# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Encyclopedia descriptions, batch M (DeepSeek)."""
DESC_M = {
    'PT:DSC2': {
        0: "Pilot of Mazinger Z.\nHe has a simple personality and is sometimes scatterbrained, but he is a hot-blooded man with a heart of justice. Entrusted with Mazinger Z by his grandfather, Dr. Juzo Kabuto, he entered battle to crush the ambitions of the evil scientist Dr. Hell, who sought world conquest.\nInitially not knowing how to handle the machine, he piloted it recklessly, but he learned through the techniques honed on his motorcycle and his innate fighting sense. These skills were also fully displayed in close-quarters combat against the Iron Mask Corps.\nAfter annihilating Dr. Hell's Mechanical Beast Corps, he entrusted the fight against the new threat, the Mikene Empire, to Tetsuya Tsurugi and Great Mazinger, and departed for America to study. However, to counter the escalating attacks of the Mikene Empire, he returned temporarily and made a comeback in a powered-up Mazinger Z, showing the gallant form of the Double Mazinger.\nAfter returning home from his studies, he boarded the TFO, which he had built independently, and the newly developed Double Spazer, throwing himself into battle against the Vega United Forces alongside Duke Fleed.\nThroughout all series, he stood against great evil - he is the true hero of justice.",
        1: "Daughter of Professor Yumi, director of the Photon Power Institute, and pilot of Aphrodai A and Dianan A.\nShe has a bright personality and is quite skilled at piloting robots and motorcycles. She also has a tomboyish side, which sometimes led her into trouble.\nShe often clashed with Kouji, but through repeated conflicts they built a relationship of trust and became what could be called the best of partners.\nAfter the battle against Dr. Hell's Mechanical Beast Corps ended, she went to America to study with Kouji. But when the war against the Mikene Empire reached its peak, she returned with Kouji and fought alongside him.",
        3: "Director of the Photon Power Institute.\nHe was Dr. Juzo Kabuto's top disciple, entrusted with full authority over the institute. He was also apparently given complete confidence, being informed of Dr. Hell's ambitions.\nHe is the leading authority in research on photon power and Super Alloy Z, and is the developer of Mazinger Z's new weapons, as well as Aphrodai A and Dianan A.\nDuring combat, he gave careful yet accurate orders to Kouji and Sayaka, and also excelled as a battle commander.\nAfter Dr. Hell's defeat, he returned to his original duties, devoting his days to peaceful research on photon power energy.",
        6: "Pilot of Great Mazinger. 18 years old.\nHe lived in an orphanage as a child, but was taken in by Dr. Kenzo Kabuto to pilot Great Mazinger. From then on, he was raised being drilled in the arts of combat, making his martial arts and robot piloting skills top-notch. However, when it came to things other than battle, his taciturn nature tended to give those around him a rough impression.\nHe looked after Shiro like a younger brother, built trusting relationships with Boss and the others, and became the pillar of the Mazinger team in place of Kouji, who had gone to America.\nWhen Kouji returned for the decisive battle against the Mikene Empire, witnessing the father-son bond between Kenzo and Kouji ignited feelings of jealousy. His refusal to cooperate with Kouji threw the Science Fortress Research Institute into crisis. What saved them was Kenzo's deep affection, no less than that of a true parent and child, but the price paid to learn that truth was far too great.",
        8: "Kouji's classmate at Tojo Academy and pilot of Boss Borot. He always has his underlings Nuke and Mucha in tow.\nHis personality is attention-seeking, a joker, and simple-minded, matching his appearance. Above all, he is weak to pretty women, and whenever a female guest appeared, he would get overly excited and become lovestruck. Naturally, he has crushes on both Sayaka and Jun.\nHe harbors an intense rivalry with Kouji, and wanting a robot he could pilot to shine in, he kidnapped the three professors of the Photon Power Institute and forced them to build Boss Borot.\nHe is always fooling around, but he genuinely possesses a desire to protect peace. While sometimes holding Kouji and Tetsuya back, he fought alongside them and built deep bonds of friendship and trust.\nAfter the war against the Mikene Empire ended, he strove to become a robot scientist, eventually reaching the point where he could modify Borot himself.",
        12: 'The pilot of Grendizer. He is the prince of the planet Fleed, which was destroyed by the Vega Star Alliance Army, and one of its survivors. He is a kind-hearted young man who wishes for peace and believes in love and friendship. He possesses high physical abilities and various psychic powers, including telepathy. Having fled from the Vega Star Alliance Army and arrived on Earth, he became the son of Doctor Umon, Daisuke, and began a new life. However, when he learned that the Vega Star Alliance Army had set its sights on Earth, he resolved to fight in Grendizer to protect Earth, his second home. After the war with the Vega Star Alliance Army ended, he set off with his sister Maria to rebuild the planet Fleed.',
        13: 'The daughter of Danbei. She is a cheerful and lively girl with the athletic ability to handle horseback riding with ease. She gradually became drawn to Daisuke, who worked at the ranch her father managed. After learning that his true identity was the alien Duke Fleed, she resolved without hesitation to fight as well. She eventually became the pilot of the Marine Spazer and supported Duke in both public and private matters. Her brightness seemed to be a salvation for Duke, who carried a dark past. However, when Duke departed to rebuild his home planet, she could not stop him and saw him off, and her love was never fulfilled.',
        14: "Duke's younger sister and princess of the planet Fleed. She is 14 years old. When the planet Fleed was attacked by the Vega Star Alliance Army, she narrowly escaped but was separated from Duke, fleeing to Earth with an elderly attendant. At first she mistakenly believed Duke was an enemy, but upon seeing the royal pendant, she was convinced he was her brother and reconciled with him. From then on, she mainly boarded the Drill Spazer and fought alongside him against the Vega Star Alliance Army. After the war with the Vega Star Alliance Army ended, she set off with Duke to rebuild the planet Fleed.",
        18: 'The absolute monarch who rules the planet Vega and the supreme commander of the Vega Star Alliance Army. He plots to dominate the entire universe, invading other planets by force and destroying any that resist, including the planet Fleed. Remaining on Vega himself, he issued orders for the Earth invasion operation from Skull Moon, the frontline base built on the Moon. But when an accident caused the planet Vega to collapse, he abandoned the citizens and fled the planet, relocating to Skull Moon. Thereafter he took direct command. In the end, he launched a full-scale attack on Earth aboard the King of Vega, but was slain by the hands of Grendizer.',
        19: "The highest authority at Skull Moon, the frontline base built on the Moon by the Vega Star Alliance Army, and the supreme commander of the Earth invasion operation. He swears absolute loyalty to Emperor Vega and strives to faithfully execute his orders. He prefers tactics of overwhelming enemies through military force. Within him lurks a female persona, 'Lady Gandal,' who has the opposite personality and favors scheming and treachery. When she voices her opinions, Gandal's face splits in two and she appears as a small woman. Later, when Gandal suffered a facial injury, reconstructive surgery was performed that replaced his face and personality entirely. As the Alliance Army's defeat became increasingly certain, Lady Gandal attempted to assassinate Emperor Vega to save herself. But sensing this, Gandal rammed his personal flagship into Grendizer to protect the Emperor and died.",
        20: 'Rubina was the daughter of Emperor Vega and the fiancee of Duke. As a child, she was sent to Planet Fleed as part of a political arrangement, and from that time she continued to love Duke. She came to Earth to inform Duke that the effects of Vega radiation were beginning to disappear from Planet Fleed, but during the battle between Zril, who had come to take her back, and Grendizer, she was gravely wounded. In the arms of her beloved, she passed away while wishing for peace to the very end.',
        22: 'Hayato, an 18-year-old youth, continued as the pilot of the Jaguar and Getter 2, and also served as the pilot of the Liger and Getter Liger. He was a high school student attending Asama Academy, and although he was the only member of the Getter Team who did not belong to an athletic club, his motor skills were outstanding. Initially, he was overconfident and built walls between himself and others, which caused constant friction within the team. However, through battle and building trust with Ryouma and the others, he came to approach matters with sincerity. His calm judgment saved the Getter from crisis on numerous occasions. The cross he always wore was a keepsake from his deceased mother, who supposedly resembled Michiru, and inside it was her photograph. When heading into a deadly mission, he handed it to Michiru and conveyed his feelings to her.',
        25: "Doctor Saotome was the director of the Saotome Research Institute and the father of Michiru and Genki. With his unshaven beard, geta sandals, and a room left in complete disarray, he gave a rather unimpressive impression. However, he was the leading authority on the mysterious radiation from space known as 'Getter Rays,' and his abilities as a scientist were recognized worldwide. He developed the Getter Robo for space development, but when the Dinosaur Empire suddenly appeared, he armed the Getter to protect the Earth. Furthermore, he completed a new combat-oriented Getter Robo to fight the Hyakki Empire. In battle, he also excelled as a commander, never losing his composure even in crisis, and supported the Getter Team with excellent situational judgment. His given name was never revealed to the end.",
        27: "Emperor Bry was the ruler of the Hyakki Empire and possessed powerful telepathic abilities. The goal of the Hyakki Empire was to implant artificial horns that served as telepathic wave receiving antennas into the heads of humanity, transforming them into Hyakki Soldiers to serve as pawns in their world conquest. However, to efficiently develop Hyakki Soldiers and Hyakki mecha, they needed a Getter Ray amplification device, and Bry relentlessly attacked the Saotome Research Institute to obtain it. He possessed the ruthlessness, cruelty, and dignity expected of his demonic appearance. All of these surpassed even those of Emperor Gore of the Dinosaur Empire. Yet he also had a lenient side toward his subordinates; when he learned that Lisa, the daughter of Hakkotsu Oni, had betrayed them, he honored Hakkotsu Oni's plea not to have to kill his own daughter and ordered someone else to execute her. Also, during the final battle, he showed consideration for Hidlar, who had just made a miraculous return, by ordering him to rest. In the end, he raised the Science Fortress Island to challenge the final battle, but was defeated before the Getter Robo.",
        28: "Marshal Hidlar was the battle commander in charge of the military forces of the Hyakki Empire. He worked alongside Doctor Gura as one of Emperor Bry's right-hand men, but behind the scenes, he was a scheming man who coveted his superior's position. He was cunning and despicable in character, showing no discrimination between friend and foe. In the past, fearing his position as marshal was threatened, he trapped General Jirai and had him executed, and when he predicted that Jirai's son Jirai Oni would become a threat, he arranged for his death in battle as well. However, he was not merely a small-time villain; he possessed considerable skill, such as breaking through the barrier of the new battleship Sea Force with his custom fighter, making a miraculous escape from an exploding Hyakki Robot, and even capturing Hayato as a prisoner during his escape. But the life he saved through that miracle was cut short when Hayato, his prisoner, destroyed the Science Fortress Island from within, ultimately costing him his life.",
        29: "Dr. Glah was a scientist who served as the brain of the Hyakki Empire. Alongside Marshal Hidler, he worked as one of Emperor Bry's right-hand men.\nHe was responsible for the development of Hyakki mecha and fighter craft, as well as the planning of operations, and his superior intellect was indispensable to the Hyakki Empire.\nUnder his tutelage, gifted young men such as Jichki and Tekkoki gathered and studied daily.\nHe was killed in action just before the final battle, but the existence of the 'Gravity Control Device' which he left behind, capable of raising even the Science Fortress Island, led Bry to decide to launch his final operation.",
        30: "Tekkoki was one of the Hyakki Hundred, the elite group of the Hyakki Empire.\nHe had absolute confidence in his own intellect, and developed the Hyakki mecha Mecha Tekkoki to defeat Getter Robo, challenging it to battle.\nHis combat ability was also first-rate, showing skill enough to fight Getter to a standstill or better. However, when Hidler's tank cut in, his pride was wounded, and he turned his blade on Hidler to protect Getter. Then, while battered and exhausted, he boldly challenged Getter to a rematch. The battle was decided by Getter Dragon's Spin Cutter, and came to a close with Tekkoki's death.",
        31: "Dokuganki was one of the Hyakki Hundred, the elite group of the Hyakki Empire.\nHe was converting dam employees and security guards into Hyakki soldiers, but since his predecessor Ikkakuki had been defeated by Getter, he took over and plotted to seize the Getter Ray amplifier.\nHe attempted to attack the Saotome Research Institute from underground, making use of his Hyakki robot's characteristics. However, while advancing underground, he was dragged out by Getter Liger and killed by four consecutive missiles.",
        32: "Gyukenki was a veteran of the Hyakki Hundred, the elite group of the Hyakki Empire.\nHe was a man of such skill that he was once called the Hero of the Sky, but due to old age he had retired from active duty. However, due to Hidler's lie that his son, Gyugaki, had been killed by Getter, he resolved to take revenge.\nEven in his old age, his skill had not waned, and with his combat-hardened experience he troubled the Getter team. But when Ryouma pointed out that 'You, who taught him nothing but fighting, are the one who killed your son,' the shock he received became the cause of his defeat.",
        33: "Toshiya Dan was the main pilot of KuRaiOh and God Sigma. He was 18 years old.\nHe was a man who loved space, believed in the future, and fought wholeheartedly for peace. Though he was from Io, he spoke with the brisk accent of an Edoite, and was a broad-minded, spirited, and passionate man who did not fuss over details.\nOn Io, he had experience helping build the ionium refinery using mining robots, and had an edge when it came to operating machines. When the Elder Army attacked and he was forced to board KuRaiOh in an emergency, he handled it as if it were an extension of his own limbs.\nHe possessed considerable combat ability even in his bare body, and his kick, especially when delivered from a jump, was ferocious.\nDuring the war with the Elders, he came to sympathize with the ideals of the enemy commander Teral, and eventually they became friends who called each other by name.\nIn the final battle, after witnessing Teral's death as his strength gave out mid-purpose, he alone cornered Gagaarn. Every bullet Gagaarn sprayed wildly in his last resistance seemed to be blocked by an unseen force, and none struck Toshiya. But the bullets Toshiya fired for his fallen comrades and for peace pierced Gagaarn for certain.\nAfter it was all over, he departed alone with God Sigma into the distant future.",
        34: "Julie Noguchi is the pilot of the sea-shaking king. He is 21 years old.\\nHe is a very cool and sharp-tongued man, and his overly accurate observations often cause trouble. However, at heart he is an upright man, and his harsh words are simply because he cannot be honest. At Trinity Base, he also serves as chief engineer, possessing intellect second only to Dr. Kazami. He is a hard worker who aims to surpass Dr. Kazami someday. His attachment to money is so strong that he could be taken for a miser, but this is because he is desperately saving up to go pick up his mother and younger sister who are on Io, revealing his deep feelings for his family. After Dr. Kazami was dazzled by Elder technology and betrayed them, he deciphered the method to release the lock on the Trinity Engine, and used the base's Trinity energy to successfully combine God Sigma, so without his intellect the Earth side's victory would not have been possible. After the battle with Gagan ended, he saw off Toshiya who was departing with the words of encouragement 'Leave Io to me.'",
        35: "Kensaku Kira is the pilot of the land-shaking king. He lost both parents before his eyes to the Elder attack, but he has a bright and straightforward personality that does not show that tragedy. However, he is a bit of a fool, a show-off, and also has a reckless side. Perhaps because their mental ages are close, he gets along especially well with Rie's younger brother Shota, and is looked up to as a big brother figure. He is a natural klutz with machines, and at first could not even pilot the land-shaking king well. But when he learned that combining into God Sigma was possible, and that the sky-shaking king would be the core unit, he climbed into the sky-shaking king, pushing Toshiya aside. However, the sky-shaking king's internal computer declared as a piloting condition: 'Fighting spirit alone is not enough. You need a cool head and trained skills.' He keenly felt his own shortcomings. After that, with his characteristic determination, he managed to at least handle the land-shaking king. When the battle with the Elder ended and Toshiya was about to depart for the future, he sent him off with the affectionate words 'Be sure to come back.'",
        36: "Rie Kasuga is Dr. Kazami's secretary and also his stepdaughter. She is a highly capable and talented woman, skillfully supporting Dr. Kazami so that the many varied duties of Trinity Base do not fall behind. She lived apart from her younger brother Shota, but later they came to live together in the base. She harbors feelings for Toshiya, and a photo of him is displayed in her room. She took over command of the entire base after departure, in place of Dr. Kazami who had opposed the base moving to Jupiter until the very end. She overcame the betrayal of the doctor she respected, fought through against the Elder army, and finally saved the Earth. Although her beloved Toshiya departed for the future, no shadow of gloom could be seen on her face as she watched him leave.",
        39: "Dr. Kazami is the genius scientist who developed Trinity energy - said to be phase energy taken from a dimensional rift - and God Sigma. He is mild-mannered and tolerant, taking in Rie who was an orphan, and treating Toshiya and the others warmly like family. His battle command using his intellect is also sound, and he is the spiritual pillar of Trinity Base. But behind that, he was captivated by Elder super-science, and had a side as a mad scientist who would capture Elder aliens and torture them to extract their secrets. This came to the surface during the torture of Teral, and afterwards he gradually began to clash with Toshiya and the others. When Trinity Base fell into crisis, he unilaterally declared defeat, sealed the Trinity Engine, and ran off alone to Gagan. Then, to seize Trinity Base as the condition offered for boarding the time ship, he turned his fangs on his former comrades. His end came when he pointed a gun at Julie who was trying to release the Trinity Engine seal, and was shot in the back by an Elder soldier. The keyword to release the seal was 'I am the genius and the world's greatest mind! I am the genius and the world's greatest mind!' - filled with Dr. Kazami's impatience with super-science and his pride as a scientist.",
        40: "Teral is the supreme commander leading the Elder army. He was dispatched to Earth in the past on orders from the Elder homeworld's senate to seize Trinity energy. He is trusted enormously by his two adjutants and many subordinates, and strives to accomplish his goals through unity. However, he encounters unexpectedly fierce resistance from God Sigma, throwing his plans into great disarray. When sending out his two subordinates who are lovers, he encourages them with particular vigor and even tries to look after them afterwards, and he is disturbed by the actions of enemies Toshiya and Rie who disregard their own safety for each other - he is weak to men and women who care for one another, and sometimes shows a somewhat feminine side. This was largely due to a secret hidden in Teral's heart and body. Later, he is stripped of his commander position by Gagan, who was sent by the senate when their patience ran out. He is driven to the brink of execution, but escapes with the help of his subordinates and reaches Earth. There, he and his former enemies Toshiya and the others come to understand each other and join hands. After the reconciliation, he acts alone, eliminating Gagan's adjutants Dalton and Mesa, and finally closes in on Gagan himself. But his strength is insufficient, and he is struck down. He entrusts the future of the Elder race to Toshiya who rushes to his side, and his soul departs on a journey to his lover.",
        42: "Jira was a commander of the Elder military under Terral, and was in charge of developing the Cosmosaurus. He was devoted to Terral, and his desire to obtain Trinity Energy felt more like it was for Terral's sake than for his homeland. He had a bitter relationship with his colleague Lietz, but he possessed the flexibility to willingly cooperate if it was for Terral's sake. After the appearance of Gagarn, who opposed Terral, he went so far as to cooperate with him throughout. When Gagarn seized full authority over the Earth attack and moved to execute Terral, Jira acted quickly and volunteered for the role of executioner, successfully placing Terral in a state of suspended animation to help him escape. He seemed to have driven off the pursuers sent by Gagarn, who had learned the full truth, in a gunfight, but he was struck in the back by a bullet from a pursuer who was still alive. At the brink of death, Terral regained consciousness and accused him of treachery, but Jira deliberately did not deny it. Then, smiling contentedly that Terral was safe, he fell into an eternal sleep. Seeing this, Terral realized the depth of Jira's loyalty and shed tears.",
        43: "Lietz was a commander of the Elder military under Terral. A brave warrior, he clashed with God Sigma many times in order to seize Trinity Energy for the sake of his homeland and Terral. However, he had an unending feud with Jira, who developed the Cosmosaurus essential to their operations. Even so, when Terral faced a crisis, they showed a surprising unity quite unlike their usual behavior. He served Terral with the loyalty of a retainer, and had even risked his life to save him from danger. When Gagarn seized full authority over the Earth attack and insulted Terral, Lietz reached his limit and cut off the head of the Lot Bird that had been set upon him. Turning his blade on Gagarn, he was blocked by Mesa's gunfire. Though his body was riddled with holes, he pressed on to within a step of his goal before his strength gave out, and he collapsed while speaking words praising Terral. His stubbornly earnest end brought tears not only to Terral's eyes, but also to those of Jira, his rival.",
        44: "Gagarn was a military man who came from the Elder homeworld under the pretext of assisting Terral. Extremely cunning and cruel by nature, he would stop at nothing to achieve his goals. His arrival in the present was not to save his homeland of Elder, but to obtain Trinity Energy, supplant the Senate, and seize control of Elder for himself. To that end, Terral's existence was an obstacle, and he employed various means to undermine his power. On one occasion, he attacked Terral's base, created a situation where they had no choice but to fight back, and then destroyed the base while claiming it was 'self-defense.' At the base, he also used force to dominate Terral's soldiers, and eventually ousted Terral to take the position of Supreme Commander of the Earth attack. However, he was not merely a villain; his abilities were extremely high. In fleet battles leading his forces, and in combat piloting the giant robot Gargos, he consistently overwhelmed God Sigma. He also possessed sharp observational skills, seeing through Terral's true identity, which even his direct subordinates Lietz and Jira had failed to notice. In the final battle within the fortress, seeing the tide turn against him, he attempted to escape alone to the future via a Time Ship, but Terral gave chase and halted him. In a gunfight, he took Terral's life and tried to flee again, but was cornered by Toshiya. In the end, he was shot through the chest, abdomen, and forehead and died.",
        45: "Dalton was Gagarn's adjutant and combat commander. His red skin, stern expression, robust physique, and overbearing attitude gave him an imposing appearance. However, his true character was pathetic: he was extremely bold when he held the advantage, but instantly turned timid the moment he fell even slightly into a disadvantage. In the battle of Io, when his ship was destroyed and he was discovered by Terral while escaping, he fell to his knees and begged for his life. When Taichirou intervened against Terral, who declared 'End your life honorably,' Dalton seized the opening and opened fire, wounding Taichirou. In the end, as he fled with his back turned, he received Terral's furious strike and vanished into the abyss.",
        46: "Mesa was Gagarn's adjutant and science chief. He created new types of Cosmosaurus and devised operations using them. Gagarn valued his excellent intellect and relied heavily on him as a right-hand man. However, he seemed to consider betrayal a virtue, having bowed his head to Terral on two occasions. The first time, his sincere attitude convinced even Terral, but once his personal safety was assured, he immediately betrayed him. The second time, he attempted to shoot Terral in the back after he had infiltrated Gagarn's fortress, but failed, and begged for his life. Given the previous incident, Terral would not accept. But when allied soldiers' covering fire caused Terral to lose his gun, Mesa promptly switched to an overbearing manner and aimed his weapon to finish him off. At that moment, a sudden shock ran through the fortress, and Terral seized a gun from a soldier in the confusion. Terral and Mesa fired simultaneously, but only Mesa was struck through the skull and died.",
        47: "Jane Noguchi was Julie's younger sister. She was a headstrong girl who, as a member of the Cosmo Factory, participated in combat alongside the men. While wounded, she happened upon Terral, who was fleeing from Gagarn's pursuers, and received treatment for her injuries from him. Through this encounter, she learned that even among the Elders, whom she had only ever seen as objects of hatred, there were those who possessed kindness, and she revised her one-sided views. Afterwards, she saved Terral's life twice: once from the Factory members who insisted he should be executed, and once from the gunfire of the Elder army soldiers pursuing him. She set out for Earth aboard a spaceship together with Terral after he disposed of the pursuers, but they were assailed by Gagarn's pursuit. With the aid of God Sigma, they barely managed to reach Earth, but she was already in a dying state due to the bullet wounds from the earlier attack and the shock of the spaceship's explosion. Telling Julie, who rushed to her side, that 'Terral is a good person,' she breathed her last in her brother's arms.",
        48: "Dan Taichirou was Toshiya's father. As the chairman of the Cosmo Factory, he served as the leader who rallied the people living on Io. After escaping the Elders' attack, he led the surviving residents in a life of flight. He was a man capable of calm judgment, unswayed by emotion or circumstance. Regarding the treatment of Terral, who was being pursued by Gagarn, when the Factory members angrily demanded his execution, Taichirou decided instead that Terral should be delivered as a prisoner to Dr. Kazami and persuaded the others to accept this. Later, cooperating with the Terral he had reunited with, he distinguished himself by repelling Gagarn's attacks until Toshiya and the others arrived at Io. He also at last met face to face with Toshiya, but collapsed due to wounds suffered during the fighting. From his sickbed, he delivered a final rallying cry to Toshiya as he engaged in a deadly struggle with Gargos, and then closed his eyes, bringing his life to an end.",
        50: "Kei Katsuragi was a young man who came to be called the Anomaly in the world sealed within the dimension of mutual interference. He was 19 years old. One might have taken him for the typical hero type - impetuous and hot-blooded - but in truth he had a frivolous nature and was an incurable womanizer. Even in the world before the space-time disruption, he had been involved with countless women, and among them, with Tina, one of his lovers, he had stolen moments of rendezvous between military duties. After being transferred to the world twenty years later, he was rescued by the Emaan Factory caravan led by Shaya and was told that he was the Anomaly. Learning that he was the cause of the world's disruption and that his existence was needed to repair it, he resolved to accompany the Factory. While primarily wooing Mimsy, he would also make passes at any woman he encountered along the way, frequently stirring up trouble. He possessed an innate piloting talent, mastering the Inertial Control System - a technology entirely unknown to him - after only a brief explanation and a little practice. He drove the Morabaa and Orguss to repel one after another the Chiram forces that sought to seize the Anomaly from Gloma. Eventually, he encountered Olson, who had also become an Anomaly, and Athena, the daughter born to him and Tina. Initially they were hostile due to their respective circumstances, but gradually they came to join hands and deepen their bonds. In the end, together with Olson, he plunged into the Great Anomaly, which had originally been a space-time vibration bomb, and within it encountered their past selves. This space-time disruption had occurred because another persona of Kei and of Olson had existed in the same time. To restore the space-time disruption, the two pulled the triggers aimed at their own past selves. In the infinite possibilities of the future shown in the epilogue, a vision of him holding a child he had fathered with Mimsy could also be seen.",
        51: "Shaya Tob was an Emaan woman serving as the chief of the Factory. She was scholarly and thoughtful, but also naive about the world and far too inclined to go at her own pace. Emaan women have a reproductive period, and once this period passes, they lose their reproductive function. However, since their physical changes also almost cease thereafter, despite already being nearly thirty years old, she still retained a youthful appearance. Furthermore, because Emaan women lose their sexual modesty once their reproductive period ends, they no longer care about exposing their bodies. When she casually entered the bath while Kei was using it, even that playboy was thoroughly taken aback. Although she came from the distinguished Tob family, she had left politics to her twin sister and was living freely with the caravan when she encountered Kei. Learning that Kei was the Anomaly needed to repair the disrupted space-time, she decided to protect him. However, this choice pained her, as it brought her into conflict not only with Chiram but also with her own younger sister, Manisha. Later, however, she succeeded in reconciling with her sister, and formed an alliance with Chiram as well for the common purpose of repairing space-time. In the infinite possibilities seen after Kei and the others plunged into the Great Anomaly, there was a vision of her nestled beside Ranchi, a former lover who had once stepped aside for her sister's sake.",
        52: "Mimsy Lass was an Emaan girl born in the century of disrupted space-time. She was 17 years old. She came from the Lass family, a distinguished house among the Emaan, and was its heiress. While gaining caravan experience as a member of the Factory, she met Kei. She already had a fiance, Sley, in the Factory, but she was drawn to the assertive Kei and her heart began to waver. As the end of her reproductive period approached, she was stricken by nightmares and collapsed. Driven by that anxiety, she confronted her own feelings honestly and at one point promised to marry Sley. But immediately afterwards, she came under attack from Manisha's pursuit forces seeking to seize Kei, and Sley, who had sortied for Mimsy's sake, lost his life. She was plunged into deep grief for a time, but eventually recovered and came to share her heart with Kei, ultimately conceiving a child with him. Like other Emaan women, Mimsy apparently also had a twin sister, but that sister seems not to have been of an active disposition and did not participate in the caravan.",
        53: "Mome was a humanoid built on Mu, indistinguishable in appearance from a human girl. After being caught in a spacetime shift and transported to Atlantis, she was put up for sale as merchandise. Katsura bought her there, and she became a member of the Gloma crew. She was designed to befriend humans, and thus possessed emotional circuits equivalent to those of a human. Because of this, she gradually came to harbor feelings of love for Katsura, her benefactor. Built for nursing and repair duties, she was capable of handling a wide range of tasks, from daily chores to mechanical maintenance. During the final battle against Mu, she channeled her own energy into the Daimora's main cannon to repel the enemy and save Mimsy. However, by the time Katsura rushed to her side, she had already exhausted all her energy, and closed her eyes in his arms. Soon after, bid farewell by Katsura's tears, she vanished into the depths of space.",
        56: "Jabby was a type of Earthling from a parallel universe with a dinosaur-like appearance. He was searching for his lover, from whom he had been separated when both were caught in a spacetime shift. He had a burner built into his mouth, and used it to drive off the Mozuku tribe, who frequently attacked by spitting fire, while on trading trips he would instead use it to attract customers. When the Gloma's trade goods were lost, his keen sense of smell once led him to discover a vineyard, making him a useful presence in many ways. He was also the one who named the Orguss. He remembered the sensation of the spacetime shifts he had experienced in the past, and could sense their approach through a reaction in his tail, which allowed the Gloma to escape danger on several occasions. As their journey continued, he finally found his homeland as he had wished. However, it had been reduced to ruins, with not only the lover he had been seeking but even his comrades all dead. Overwhelmed by despair at the devastation, he wished to stay behind alone and die. Yet, persuaded by Katsura, he changed his mind and returned to the Gloma, which had become his second home.",
        57: "League was a technician at the Factory. When the Bronco II that Katsura had been riding was destroyed, League used his considerable technical skill to repair and modify it, creating the Orguss. After the alliance with Chiram, he worked together with Chiram's technicians to complete the spacetime conversion device.",
        58: "Slay was an Emaan man and a member of the Factory. Weak and slender of build, he gave an androgynous impression. He was Mimsy's fiance, and wished to be united with her before her secondary sexual characteristics, which would allow her to bear children, came to an end, but she would not accept him, and he was at his wit's end. Then Katsura suddenly appeared and began courting Mimsy, so Slay directed his hostility at Katsura, once even working through Shaya to have him expelled. His feelings for Mimsy were genuine; when she was nearly carried off by a Mozuku warrior, he picked a fight he was clearly outmatched in to protect her. He left the caravan for a time, but returned to the Gloma just as Mimsy's reproductive window was about to close. He promised marriage to Mimsy, who called his name in her delirium, and shook hands with Katsura as well. Just as it seemed everything would be settled peacefully, they were struck by Manisha's pursuit force. He sortied in the Orguss II to protect Mimsy, but was soon hit. Then, resolved, he rammed his craft into the enemy ship and fell in battle, never having been united with Mimsy.",
        59: "Gove was an old man who accompanied the Factory. He was a true merchant of the stripe who would unblinkingly engage in shady dealings, such as palming off scraps of combat mecha to ignorant Atlantans as precious gems. He seemed to get along well with Katsura, drinking with him and playing a game similar to Othello. When Mimsy became pregnant, he again proposed the name 'Gamon' for the child, the same name he had suggested when the Orguss was being named. Why he was so attached to that name was unknown.",
        61: "Born in Mu 200 years ago, this robot warrior was designed for infantry combat and close-to-mid-range ground warfare. Its rank, needless to say, is Captain. It served as a combat commander in the 11th Combat Platoon of the 22nd Battalion of the Esrina Front Army, but during battle it was caught up in a space-time shift and thrown to the Europe region, where its activity ceased. When Gargos fled to Europe to escape Chiram, it was found by Kei and Mome, who were searching for reusable junk, and was repaired, becoming a member of the Gargos crew. Its excessive pride often hindered rapid action, and it disliked using Emaan weapons, frequently failing to stay in step with those around it. However, once it became serious, its combat ability was remarkable. When Kei and the others made their push into the Great Anomaly, it exposed itself to gunfire to hold back Mu's fierce assault. It seemed to have followed after Mome, but it barely survived, and went on to face an even stranger fate. That, however, is an episode that should be told in another story.",
        63: "Born on February 20 of Year 2 of the Chaotic Time-Space Century, she is the daughter of Kei and Tina. She is 18 years old. From the age of 11 she enlisted as a child soldier in the Chiram military and worked as a soldier. She met Olson when he was placed under the protection of her grandfather Michael, and she saw in him the ideal image of a father. When her mother and grandfather were later killed in a Mu attack, she resolved to fight not for revenge, but so that no more people would have to taste the same sorrow she had known. She volunteered for a transfer to the front lines and was drilled in combat techniques by Olson. As a result, the delicacy of a woman combined with the bloodline of a genius pilot gave birth to a first-rate female warrior. Towards her father, whose face she had never seen, she harbored loneliness at his absence and resentment over the hardships he had caused her grandfather and mother. Later, even when Olson told her that the Anomaly Chiram was targeting was in fact her real father, her long-nurtured anger made her stubbornly deny it. When she heard that Kei had fathered a child with Mimsy, her irritation only grew. However, when the mission to protect the Anomaly was later handed down, she suppressed her personal feelings and faithfully carried out the mission. During that time the awkward parent and child clashed repeatedly, each time drawing sighs from Olson. But when she was wounded, Kei was there at her bedside, devoting himself to her care. That incident seemed to dissolve the ill will, and when she sortied again, she wore Emaan clothes instead of the Chiram military uniform. Just before Kei plunged into the Great Anomaly, she at last called him 'Father' and handed him a pendant containing a photo of Tina. At the same time, she had been entrusted by Olson with his sunglasses as a keepsake.",
        65: "A young man who came to be called the other Anomaly in a world sealed by the clashing spheres. He was born in the same year as Kei, but having appeared in the Chaotic Time-Space five years earlier than Kei, his lived age was also five years older, making him 25. Upon appearing in the Chaotic Time-Space Century, he was taken under the protection of General Michael Henderson of the Chiram military. Through that connection he met the general's beloved daughter Tina and his granddaughter Athena. After Tina and Michael died in a Mu attack, he became Athena's guardian and instructor, supporting her in both public and private matters without ever revealing his hidden feelings. As a key figure known as the Anomaly, and with his pre-Chaotic Time-Space achievements recognized, he received the unprecedented rank of Special Major General in the Chiram military. He initially clashed with Kei as well, but once Chiram pushed forward with a space-time repair plan that did not use the Anomaly, he left the military and returned to sharing the same pot of rice with Kei again. In the end he entered the Great Anomaly together with Kei and confronted his past self, pulling the trigger to bring an end to the chaos. Among the infinite possibilities of the future shown in the epilogue, there was also a scene of him exchanging a kiss with Athena.",
        66: "Commander of the Chiram military's Tran garrison. His rank is Captain. As a veteran of many battles, he is the type to cling to honors and military achievements. Initially he acted to seize Kei, the Anomaly, but as orders changed his objective shifted to assassination. He persistently pursued both Kei and Olson, who had become a traitor, but each time he met with failure. About to be removed from his command for his constant inability to complete his mission, he pressed his superior Wesley along with his subordinates, pleading for the mission to continue. Seizing his last chance, he went to the front lines himself. In the decisive battle fought with his back to the wall, he launched a fierce assault on Manisha's fleet, which was trying to protect Kei and Olson, but was shot down by Olson, who had sortied out. He was persuaded to reconsider Plan D but would not listen, and as he was regrouping for another attack he took the main cannon of the Gargos, entrusted his legacy to Henry, and died in the explosion.",
        67: "Deputy commander of the Chiram military's Tran garrison. Calm and composed by nature, he ably supported his beloved commander Roberto. In the operation to seize the Anomaly he always led from the front, but failures piled up. When he was about to be relieved of his post, he half-coerced his superior Wesley into allowing the mission to continue, and seized the last chance. But in the desperate final battle he lost Roberto and was forced into a bitter retreat. Afterwards he showed his obsession by deserting the military to continue chasing Kei and Olson. He launched an attack after Emaan and Chiram had formed a joint force, but a missile strike from a force dispatched by Wesley brought him down with his goal unachieved.",
        68: "Manisha Tove is Shaya's twin sister. Her elder sister, who should be the head of the family, is away on a wandering merchant's journey, so Manisha serves as the de facto head of the Tove household in her place. She came into conflict with Mimsy's family, the Lars household, over the treatment of Katsuragi, and asked Katsuragi to undertake time-space restoration centered on Emaan. However, her forceful methods provoked resistance, and her proposal was refused. When she then showed a willingness to brainwash Katsuragi, she came into conflict with her own sister as well. She continued to pursue Gloma afterward, but was shocked when Mimsy revealed that her husband Lanch had once favored Shaya, and that Shaya had stepped aside for Manisha's sake. Furthermore, at a discussion meeting, she heard her sister's sincere words that saving the Earth should take priority over Emaan's future, and at last she was reconciled with Shaya.",
        70: "Wesley is the commander of the Chiram military's front-line base, with the rank of lieutenant general. He attempted to relieve Roberto's team of their mission to eliminate the Anomaly after their repeated failures, but gave them one last chance after receiving a plea that bordered on blackmail. Later, after Emaan and Chiram formed an alliance, Henry appeared intent on destroying the Anomaly even at the cost of breaking from military control, so Wesley dispatched reinforcements and had him eliminated.",
        72: "Marin Reigan is a special member of Blue Fixer's special combat unit and the pilot of New Palsaverne and Baldios. As an alien, he was initially suspected of being a spy and faced strong hostility within the base. However, through his actions he gradually won trust, and with his superior piloting skill and knowledge of subspace mechanics, he was finally made the main pilot of Baldios. He is a man of conviction who always carries out what he believes is right, and he will rush to the aid of comrades and loved ones in crisis even at the cost of disobeying orders. But that conviction is a double-edged sword that can also become a liability. This was revealed when he was willing to kill Marie, the news bureau chief of the world broadcast, to protect the secret of Baldios when she tried to investigate the Blue Fixer base. In truth, however, he is a pure-hearted young man who loves the beauty of the Earth more than Earthlings themselves. For that very reason, his obsession with defeating Gattler is fierce, and his anger toward Aldebaron, who would engulf the Earth in war, burns like a raging fire within his heart. He seems oblivious in matters of love: when Jamie invited him to a concert, he showed up at the meeting place with Raita and Oliver in tow, hurting her feelings with such a careless response. Though he was opposed to Aphrodia, their exchanges through battle touched a chord in his heart. In time, his heart was drawn toward her, but the war would claim Aphrodia's life. In the unaired final episode of the TV series, after parting from Gattler as they departed for a new star, he returned alone to Earth, where he was greeted by the phantoms of Aphrodia and Raita. In the theatrical version, after descending to a Earth polluted by radiation, he cradled the lifeless Aphrodia in his arms and walked toward the lighthouse where the two had apparently first met.",
        73: "Oliver Jack is a corporal in Blue Fixer's special combat unit and the pilot of Baldiprize. He is 22 years old. Born in a slum, his parents separated when he was ten, so he and his younger sister Emily were placed in an institution. He volunteered for the Blue Fixer Boys' Corps at age twelve, and Raita, whom he met there, has been his close friend ever since. He is cheerful and wears his emotions on his sleeve, with a delinquent streak, and he will resist to the end anything he cannot stomach. When captured by Aldebaron and nearly turned into a spy through a mind-control device, he resisted by cutting himself with a knife to stay sane. Having survived a poor and turbulent boyhood, when Aldebaron withered the Earth's crops and caused food shortages, he erupted in anger at the World Federation's methods of suppressing rioters by force, and led an attack on the Federation's warehouses himself. Yet he is by no means a crude person: he keeps a Bible at hand as his treasured companion and secretly harbors feelings for Jamie, revealing a pure side. When Aldebaron's plan to destroy humanity brought a great flood upon the Earth, he trembled with frustration at being unable to save Emily and her family, and wept alone over her letter.",
        74: "Raita Hokuto is a sergeant in Blue Fixer's special combat unit and the pilot of the Catallenger. He is 21 years old and also serves as a part-time instructor at the military academy's night school. He is from the facility 'Little Japan' built at point M-29 on the Moon, and is the sole survivor of a spaceship accident that killed all aboard. Raised afterward in a foster home, he joined the Blue Fixer Boys' Corps at age eleven, went through the military academy, and was assigned to the Blue Fixer unit. He is a stubborn man of solid character and deep sentiment, who dislikes sending others on dangerous missions and bravely volunteers himself. When Marin first joined the unit, Raita did not trust him at all, and their arguments often escalated into fistfights. However, as they faced death together, he came to feel Marin's resolve firsthand and trusted him from the bottom of his heart. In the unaired episode 38, he went to deal with nuclear missiles seized by the enemy, completed the mission, but was fatally wounded by Gattler's attack. Despite his efforts, Gattler, fearing Baldios, launched the remaining nuclear missiles, and the Earth was polluted with radiation.",
        75: "Jemmy Hoshino is an 18-year-old member of the applied physics research laboratory belonging to the science development bureau of the World Federation's Blue Fixer. From a young age, she lived alone with her mother, but after her mother's death, she was raised by a Japanese-Greek family. After the death of her foster parents, she entered an institution, and at age 15 volunteered for the World Federation military.\nHer emotional expressions are clear and direct, and she cannot abandon people in need. She normally works under Quinstein, but depending on the mission, she is an active girl who willingly joins Marin and the others in actual combat.\nHer father's identity was unknown, but during a mission to the Bird Kingdom, the truth came to light that the Bird King was in fact her father.\nHer early conviction that Marin was a trustworthy person shows that she possesses extremely keen sensibility. It may have been inevitable that, through her loving care touching his pure and lonely heart and gradually untangling it, she came to be drawn to him. However, since Marin always had his eyes on Aphrodia, her romantic feelings never came to fruition.",
        76: "Goji Tsukikage is the commander of Blue Fixer, an independent organ of the World Federation. He is 40 years old and formerly served as chief of the World Federation Far East branch.\nInitially treating Marin as a spy, he was moved by Marin's feelings for Earth and welcomed him into Blue Fixer as a comrade in arms.\nHis position tends to make him too hard on himself - even when news of his wife and children's crisis in Japan arrived, he suppressed his desire to rescue them and tried to ignore it. He is also a good leader with the fairness to voice his opinions without fear of rank or position when someone clearly acts wrongly.\nHe also showed consideration for his subordinates, such as holding birthday parties to reward the hard-working Blue Fixer members. To the members, he is not just a superior but almost a father figure. Away from work, however, he is an ordinary middle-aged man whose hobbies are watching classic films and jogging every morning.\nIn the unaired episode 34, he sortied in a Mini Palsaburn to rescue Marin and the others on a suicide mission carrying melted-down nuclear material into subspace from the undersea base battle, saving both Earth and the young people by ramming the Spirit Gattler I together with the nuclear material.",
        77: "Ella Quinstein is a scientist attached to Blue Fixer and director of the science development bureau. She is 32 years old.\nAs a leader supporting Blue Fixer from the technical side, she developed various machines, led by the Baldiprize and Catallenger. Most notably, her concept and technical skill in analyzing and modifying the Palsaburn - the culmination of subspace engineering on Planet S-1 - to build Baldios shows extraordinary scientific ability and capability.\nShe previously held a post at the Sunbridge University research laboratory, but resigned when the World Federation issued a suspension order for her joint research with her mentor and lover Nerd, citing 'risk of military application.' Afterward, she volunteered for the World Federation military and has been devoting herself to Earth's defense.\nShe is a resolute and quiet woman who suppresses her emotions and devotes herself to her duties. She is strict with both herself and others, and did not hesitate to shoot dead Nerd when he misused her earlier research achievement, the 'Vacuum Box,' as a weapon. Yet she answered the final wish of her student Devitt heading toward certain death, proving without doubt that she is truly a deeply emotional person.\nAmong members who suspected Marin of being an alien spy, she was also one with a sure eye, quickly recognizing his knowledge of subspace mechanics and high piloting skill, and requesting his cooperation as Baldios' pilot.\nAfter Commander Tsukikage's death, she serves as acting commander of Blue Fixer to carry on his will. In the theatrical version, she boarded Baldios together with Jemmy for direct command in the final battle at Saturn.",
        78: "Devitt Wayne is a pilot candidate for the World Federation Blue Fixer special combat unit.\nHe came to the Blue Fixer base as the second pilot of the New Palsaburn.\nHis nihilistic air and provocative tone easily invite misunderstanding, but in essence he is a hot-blooded man who would not hesitate to throw away his life for a goal.\nHe is Quinstein's former student and has harbored romantic feelings for her since his school days. However, knowing those feelings will never be requited, he is tormented.\nTo destroy the satellite Ganymede, which Aldebaron had moved to block sunlight, he volunteered to board the suicide weapon Fixer 1 in Marin's place. His motive was not to protect Earth but to protect only Quinstein, just one person.\nOn the night before sortie, he confessed his feelings to Quinstein and had his wish to spend the night together accepted. When he visited her room at the appointed time, however, he was satisfied that she had accepted him, and sortied without seeing her, as if cutting off his feelings. By the time he headed toward Ganymede, not a trace of regret remained in his heart.\nHis looks and manner of death made him a character of considerable popularity during the original broadcast. In the later theatrical version, he was treated quite favorably, even boarding Baldios albeit temporarily.",
        79: "Rosa Aphrodia is the supreme commander of Aldebaron. She is 25 years old.\nAt age 13 she lost both parents in a traffic accident, and she and her younger brother Milan were raised by Gattler. At 23 she became captain of Gattler's palace guard, and after the successful coup she attained her present position. She holds strong trust and loyalty toward Gattler, and even when a classmate from the military academy told her that Gattler had assassinated her parents, her heart never wavered.\nHer ability as a commander is exceptional, and she single-handedly handles everything from operational planning to on-site command in Gattler's place. She also established the 'merciless precept' that failure must be atoned with death, and has a cold side that traps and murders those who stand in her and Gattler's way. However, many resent that she holds the position of supreme commander merely as the Fuhrer's confidante.\nWhen the Reigan research institute was attacked, her beloved younger brother Milan was killed by Marin, and she came to hate him fiercely. As a result, when facing Marin she would forget her usual composure and be swept away by passion.\nYet as she came into contact with Marin's purity in battle, she gradually began to feel something stronger than hatred. As those feelings swelled, her heart wavered between her duty as supreme commander, her reverence for Gattler, and her love-hate toward Marin.\nIn the unaired portion of the TV version, she was driven from Aldebaron by Negroth's treachery, and challenged battle alone to exact revenge but was defeated. In the later theatrical version, she was taken prisoner by Blue Fixer but escaped and vanished, only to appear at the final battle in the subspace fortress, where she killed Gattler with her own hands. And while the paths differed, in both versions she drew her last breath in the arms of the Marin she loved.",
        80: "Zeo Gattler is the supreme commander of the Aldebaron military. He also holds the positions of chairman of the unified council and chairman of the joint chiefs of staff, making him the de facto dictator who controls the S-1 people. He is 38 years old.\nNot only does he possess high ability as a soldier, but his charisma and drive allow him to quickly win the hearts of the people, and he is a leader of considerable caliber.\nOn planet S-1, he served as captain of the imperial guard for Emperor Trinomias III, and repeatedly petitioned for escape from the radiation-contaminated planet. However, impatient with the emperor, who respected the opinions of scientists seeking to restore the environment, he used the Aldebaron military to carry out the emperor's assassination. He then framed Marin for the crime and had the troublesome scientists executed.\nAfter the success of the coup, he declared the evacuation of S-1, loaded the citizens aboard the giant battleship Algol, and carried out a warp to a new world. When he decided to make Earth, the first habitable planet discovered, their new home world, he ordered an attack to exterminate the human race.\nHe is tolerant of his allies, but he also has a heartless side, not hesitating to discard failed subordinates to accomplish his goals. But this too was for the mission he had imposed upon himself to save the S-1 people, and his steel will was never bent to the very end.\nHe dotes on Aphrodia, who is both his subordinate and like a daughter to him, and places immense trust in her. For this reason, he entrusted her with full authority over the Earth invasion, while he himself awaited news of the operation's success in a subspace fortress.\nLater, however, taking over from Aphrodia who was having difficulty conquering Earth, he took command of a grand scheme to annihilate humanity by melting the polar ice caps and submerging the land. When the resulting rise in sea level made Earth's geography resemble S-1 exactly, even the bold man could not hide his surprise.\nIn the unaired episode featuring the Saturn decisive battle, he lost most of the S-1 people who had departed their home world together. Then, leading the few compatriots remaining in the cryogenic area, he set off to search for a new world.",
        81: "Negros is one of the staff officers of the Aldebaron military.\nHe shows a posture of submission to Gattler, but he is an ambitious man who schemes to topple him from the position of supreme commander and stand at the apex of the S-1 people, should the opportunity arise.\nHe deeply hates Aphrodia, who left his twin brother Gallo to die in the Himalayas. Therefore, using the relationship between Earth and S-1 that Gattler kept hidden as a shield, he dragged Aphrodia down from her position as commander-in-chief and took her place.\nIn the TV version, he dies in an explosion from Harman's suicide attack, but in the theatrical version he was given a more important role. In the final battle, even with defeat certain, he attempts to press the nuclear missile launch button to strike back at the Earth side. This act incurs Gattler's wrath, and he is killed on the spot. However, because he fell onto the nuclear missile launch button, the missiles were launched. The radiation-contaminated Earth began to transform into a new S-1.",
        82: "Flick Kyarin is an Aldebaron officer who secretly leaked allied information to Blue Fixer.\nHe was a childhood friend of Marin, and the two studied together at UF Museion, the university of planet S-1. However, a dispute over the acquisition of a bachelor's degree put a rift in his friendship with Marin, and he disappeared from Marin's sight thereafter.\nNow, in order to avenge the comrades who were executed during the Aldebaron coup, he enlisted in the military and awaited his chance for revenge. When he obtained the location of an important secret factory, he contacted Marin, hoping to defect to Earth. There was no longer any discord between the two upon their reunion, and they swore to each other to defeat Gattler.\nHowever, the information itself was a trap set by Aphrodia, and the two were trapped in a hyper-warped space. To save Baldios, he came up with the idea of using the explosion of Silver Shark to erase the distortion, and deliberately played the villain, attacking Baldios. Though Marin knew his friend's true intent, he was left with no choice but to go along with it, and Silver Shark was destroyed by Marin's hand, allowing Baldios to escape by the skin of its teeth.",
        84: 'Kamikita Kappei is the second son of the Kamikita family and the main pilot of Zambot 3. He is 12 years old and a first-year middle school student.\nHe is a well-known delinquent in his area, spending his days fighting and riding motorcycles without a license. However, his nature is kind, and he is a man of sentiment who cannot ignore those in trouble.\nWith piloting skills acquired through sleep learning, his natural athleticism, and his keen intuition, he controls Zambird, Zambo Ace, and Zambot 3 as if they were parts of his own body. He grew increasingly frustrated, however, that even as he desperately fought Gaizock, the people around him would not understand. But through witnessing the escalating destruction and inhuman tactics such as human bombs, and through reconciling with those he had clashed with, he grew as a person.\nIn the final battle, even reduced to Zambo Ace alone, he destroyed Gaizock and, unconscious, returned alone to his birthplace. He awoke in the lap of Michi amid a cheering crowd, gazing up at a universe where war was no more.',
        85: "Kamikita Uchuta is the eldest son of the Kamikita family and the pilot of Zambull. He is 15 years old and a third-year middle school student.\nHe has a cynical air and appearance, but like Kappei, his nature is warm. He is intellectual and quick-witted, and on occasion contributed to victory by devising strategies. He has a younger brother named Kazuyuki and a younger sister named Kiiro, and both look up to him as a good older brother.\nUnlike the rest of the Kami family, he has a mother who could be called a 'pushy mother', and he felt a sense of debt toward her for trying to protect only her own life and household possessions without regard for the situation around them. He clashed with Kappei over this, but through battle their bond deepened.\nIn the final battle, caught in Bandock's ferocious assault and realizing that neither he nor his machine would last much longer, he and Keiko made a suicide charge at the thruster nozzles to open a path. Even facing death, he showed a kindness that put others before himself, apologizing to Keiko that if he had only moved alone, she would not have been caught up in it. Then, amid the rising debris, crying out Kappei's name as if entrusting his feelings to him, he vanished into space.",
        86: "She is the eldest daughter of the Kamikita family and the pilot of the Zambe Base. She is a 13-year-old (until episode 11) second-year middle school student. Her family runs a ranch in Shinshu, and her specialties are horseback riding and archery, making her an active and generous beautiful girl. She has a younger sister named Kimiko, but Kimiko is introverted and completely unlike her in appearance.\nOn her birthday, when she returned to her hometown, she was resented by her friends like the other Kam family members, and showed weakness in being shocked by this. However, she recovered through her mother's love, and her figure continuing rescue operations despite injuries from stray bullets led her friends to clear up their misunderstandings and approach her. This inner strength is her true essence.\nDuring the decisive battle against Bandock, when she saw that combat with Zambot 3 was impossible, she detached the still-functional Zambo Ace and, along with Uchuta, carried out a suicide attack on the thruster port to open a path. Even at the brink of death, she showed composure in admonishing Uchuta, who apologized for involving her in the attack. But in her final moments, there was the figure of a girl her age calling out her father's and mother's names.",
        87: "He holds the position of elder of the Kam family, uniting the clan under strong will and conviction as they face the battle against Gaizock. He and Umee, a good advisor, are cousins, and the fact that he gave her a tea bowl in his youth suggests they were quite close. In the end, he carried out a suicide attack against Bandock in Beal II alongside Umee to save King Beal from crisis. Entrusting the future to the younger generation, he closed the curtain on his life. He also handled the narration for the next episode previews, and his closing line, 'Well then, how will we fight through?' was memorable. After his suicide attack, the line was changed to the third-person perspective, 'Well then, how will they fight?'",
        88: "Kappei's father. 48 years old. He is a fishing fleet owner running Kami Fisheries in Suruga Bay. After Beal I was discovered, he served as its captain and directed combat operations. Though strict in character, his love for his wife and children runs deep, and he is a man of the sea full of tolerance and gallantry. Because he was often away from home for deep-sea fishing, he knew the importance of time spent with family. His end was a fierce one: he rammed the Red Knight Deathkaine and Blue Knight Helldyne, taking them with him and protecting his beloved wife to the last.",
        89: "Kappei's older brother. 17 years old. In contrast to his younger brother, he has a serious and gentle personality. He handles combat command for Beal I and King Beal. He possesses sharp insight and discovered the combination system of Zambot 3. On that occasion, to admonish Kappei and the others who were not working together, he stopped Zambo Ace's movements and threatened, 'Kappei without solidarity and a Kam family that cannot fight are unnecessary, so let's all die together,' getting them to agree to combine - a bold and resourceful action. After the conclusion with Gaizock, he barely survived, but he slowed down Bandock as it entered the atmosphere using Beal I, and after rescuing Kappei, who was left behind inside, he himself was swallowed by the flames of the explosion and departed this world.",
        90: "Kappei's grandmother. 68 years old. She holds a position of advisor to the Kam family, and Heizaemon places complete trust in her. Her favorite music is rock, and she once donned a combat suit and sortied out herself to save Nozaki, her first love - a vigorous grandmother who shows no signs of her age. When she went into space for the decisive battle, she carried out a suicide attack against Bandock in Beal II alongside Heizaemon to save King Beal, which had fallen into crisis. Entrusting the future to her grandchildren, she lowered the curtain on her life. Before that sortie, she left behind the tea bowl that Heizaemon had given her in her youth, a keepsake of memories.",
        91: "Kappei's mother. 35 years old. She is a boisterous and generous woman, as her appearance suggests. She shows love for her two sons and husband, and when Kazuki fired a gun out of misplaced resentment, she did not fear the weapon and slapped him, displaying the strength and maternal nature to correct wrongdoings. Just before the final battle with Gaizock, she was sent back to Earth by the older men who did not want women and children involved in the fighting. When Kappei survived the battle and returned, she rushed to his side.",
        92: "Kappei's beloved dog. It was named Chiyonishiki after the flower-petal pattern on its forehead. When sortieing, it rides in the right cockpit of the Zambird alongside Kappei. Eventually, it came to handle Kappei's shout of 'One!' during combination. When Zambo Ace penetrated the interior of Bandock, it was vaporized by a direct hit from the laser of the automatic defense system.",
        93: "The leader of the delinquent gang Kazuki-gumi, which was in conflict with Kappei. When the Gaizock attacked, he was separated from his parents and his younger sister Kaoru. Believing the Kami Family was responsible for this, he harbored intense hatred. However, witnessing the cruel tactics of the Gaizock, such as human bombs, he gradually changed his views. Eventually he found himself in a crisis where he nearly became a human bomb himself, but escaped danger thanks to Kappei's efforts. After exchanging a warm handshake with the reunited Kappei, he began to cooperate, and went up to space, the site of the final battle, alongside the Kami Family. Just before the final battle with Gaizock, he was sent back to Earth by the older men who did not want women and children involved, and upon waking he lamented that he wanted to fight together. After the battle ended and Kappei returned, he was the first to find him along with Miti, and watched over his sleeping face trembling with fear.",
        94: 'A member of the delinquent gang Kazuki-gumi, which was in conflict with Kappei. While evacuated with Kazuki and the others, he was captured by the Gaizock and unknowingly modified into a human bomb. He tried to die in a place where he would not cause trouble to those around him, but could not endure the fear of dying alone and went into a frenzy. Restrained by others who had also been made into human bombs, he screamed for help as he exploded.',
        95: "One of the members of the so-called 'Bosu Pea', Kappei's personal guard. 12 years old. She and her family were caught in a Gaizock attack and suffered damage, with her mother sustaining serious injuries. She blamed the Kami Family for this and vented fierce anger at Kappei. But deep down she understood that the real culprits were not Kappei and the others, and with her mother's words she gradually reconciled. Eventually she was captured by the Gaizock, but was rescued by Kappei. However, by that time, her body had already been modified into a human bomb. She was brought to Kappei's room, put on his pajamas, and just when it seemed their feelings would finally unite, at the moment before Kappei, alerted by Heizaemon of the possibility of a human bomb, rushed to the room, her body was enveloped in light. All that remained of her was a scrap of pajama fabric in Kappei's hand.",
        96: "Michi is a member of Kappei's guard, commonly known as one of the 'Boo Spare.' Her family was caught in a Gaizock attack and suffered damage, and believing the Kamikami family to be responsible, she vented her anger at Kappei. Like Aki, she was captured by Gaizock, but before being turned into a human bomb, she was rescued by Kazuki's hand and narrowly escaped. After the battle ended, she gently embraced Kappei, who had returned to Earth unconscious. At that moment, her pent-up feelings were pointed out by Kazuki, and her cheeks reddened.",
        97: "Killer the Butcher is the captain of the Bandock and the commander of the Gaizock forces. He is a cyborg whose body has been almost entirely replaced with machinery. Originally from a frontier planet, he became a subordinate of the Gaizock God (Computer Doll No. 8) and, following its instructions, plotted the annihilation of the human race. He has a cruel personality and treats slaughter as a hobby, carrying out one inhumane operation after another, including human bombs. At the same time, he shows a strong interest in Earth's culture and entertainment. His objects of interest changed each time - he had designers tailor costumes for him, indulged in pachinko, sunbathed, and even formed a band and sang passionately. These comical aspects stood in stark contrast to his ruthlessness and were seen on many occasions. When the Kamikami family closed in on the Bandock at the end of the fighting, he separated the Bandock's head and took to the battlefield himself. Upon receiving the Ion Cannon from Zambot 3 and realizing his defeat, he left behind the parting words that 'the Kamikami family's fight is meaningless' and crumbled away.",
        100: "Computer Doll No. 8 is the electronic brain that serves as the true body of the Gaizock, residing at the core of the Bandock. After destroying the planet Beal 200 years ago, it halted its activities. When it drew near Earth's sphere, it reactivated its program and issued orders to Butcher to eradicate humanity. Its true nature was an artificial intelligence created long ago by the Gaizock people with the purpose of driving out all beings with malice throughout the universe. Even when it faced Zambo Ace after losing the battle, it continued to insist to Kappei until the very end that humanity was evil, and then it collapsed.",
        101: "Banjo Haran is the pilot of Daitarn 3. Known in all places, he is the so-called 'Legendary Banjo Haran.' He is 18 years old. Cheerful and bright, full of a spirit of humor, he is a reliable man who never forgets a joke even in a pinch. His conceited and self-confident nature does not come across as unpleasant thanks to the very human sides he occasionally reveals. His physical abilities are outstanding, and he is capable of fighting Mega Noids on equal terms with his bare body. Because of his ferocity, rumors sometimes circulate that Banjo himself is a Mega Noid. He fiercely hates the Mega Noids and his father, who created them and used his older brother and mother as test subjects. He possesses a ruthlessness that would not hesitate to sacrifice comrades in order to destroy the Mega Noids, yet his comrades place tremendous trust and affection in him, including for that very trait. During the decisive battle against Don Zauser, the leader of the Mega Noids, Banjo listened to the apology of his creator but rejected it, and alone brought an end to his feud with the Mega Noids. Note that the 'Haran Zaibatsu,' which frequently appeared in the old SRW series, is an original game setting; in the show itself, he remains merely a very wealthy man.",
        106: "Jiron Amos is a civilian boy who charges forward single-mindedly, faithful to his own convictions. He is 16 years old. Breaking the 'Three-Day Law' established by the Innocent, which states that any crime becomes void after three days have passed, he continued to pursue Timp, the murderer of his parents. On the way, he met Rag and the others, and together they tried to steal the Xabungle they happened to come across. Though they ultimately failed, he subsequently ended up boarding the Iron Gear by circumstance. He is full of power that cannot be contained by merely calling him proactive - once he sets his mind on something, he charges through to the end. At first glance he seems merely reckless, but that very attitude was the embodiment of the 'strong civilian' that the Innocent had longed for over generations. That influence spread to those dissatisfied with the current state of affairs, and ultimately led to the defeat of Kasim King, the root of all evil. He is quite skilled at piloting Walker Machines, and he sometimes even taught Blume and the others. However, that instruction was only basic level; more than excelling at fine techniques, he more often got through by force. With his round face, joker demeanor, crude and thoughtless personality, by any ordinary standard he hardly seems the type to be popular with girls. Yet perhaps because he was unconventional in every way, he was quite popular with the girls around him. However, when Arthur appeared, he was suddenly driven from that position. After the defeat of the Innocent, he made a manly confession, declaring he would become the eyes of the blinded Elche, and won her heart. And then, together with his comrades, and those who were not quite so, he rode off across the wasteland.",
        107: "Elche Cargo is the captain of the Iron Gear, and she is sixteen years old. Her father, the trader Cargo, was killed in battle, and against her own wishes she was forced to succeed him in his role. She longs for the cultured life of the Innocent and dreams of bringing the flower of civilization to the earth. However, she is hardly what one would call demure; rather, she is quick-tempered and skilled with throwing knives, being more of a tomboy. Even so, she seems to be quite self-conscious about her personality deep down. Eventually she falls in love with the unconventional Jiron and begins a rivalry with Rag over him. Yet she is abducted by the Innocent, who have taken notice of the new-age civilian, and the personality of Kashiim is implanted into her brain. Under mental control, Elche becomes an enemy of the Iron Gear and stands in Jiron's path time and again. When she is finally rescued, Arthur's desperate gambit of drawing Kashiim's personality into his own brain restores her sense of self, and with that momentum she becomes one of the causes that bring an end to the era ruled by the Innocent. After the fighting concludes, she is troubled by the trouble she caused everyone, and despite having lost her sight as an aftereffect of the battle, she slips away from the Iron Gear alone. But the kindness and love of Jiron, who pursues her, touches her and shatters her resolve to run away.",
        109: "Fatman Big is Elche's loyal attendant and bodyguard. He was once forced to work like a slave under the corrupt locksmith Giran, until Elche bought him out. Since then, he has sworn absolute loyalty to her. His physical abilities are exceptional, including the monstrous strength from his muscular build and his surprising agility. When Elche falls into crisis, these abilities are further enhanced, allowing him to display superhuman power. After Elche is taken by the Innocent, he is even more determined to fight for her sake, and he boards the Gear Gear alone to rescue her. Even afterward, he continues to interact with Elche through every means available to him in an effort to help her regain her memories.",
        113: "Chiru is a member of the Sandrat bandit group. She carries a bear-shaped pouch and serves as something of a mascot, but she performs her work professionally and without fail. Her remarks sharply pointing out the psychology of others reveal her deep insight and mature mental age. Still, when she cries out in moments of peril, she seems every bit her age. According to Jiron, she will 'grow into a fine woman someday'.",
        117: "Timmp Sharon is the breaker who killed Jiron's parents. He seemed to be a drifter, but in truth he was an agent of the Innocent, who instigate battles between civilians under the guise of trials. His cunning, his mastery of Walker Machine piloting, and his quick draw with a gun are all top-notch, and his bearing carries the air of a true big shot. Yet there is a certain absent-mindedness about him, and he provided many comical moments, such as burning his nose with the cigar he kept in his mouth. He fought fierce battles time and again against Jiron, who pursued him for revenge, and when he finally seemed to have been defeated at Jiron's hands, he once managed to survive the crisis by playing dead. In the end, he survived to the very last, and he was still in fine form in the final scene.",
        118: 'Kid Hola is a breaker who works as an agent of the Innocent. He was formerly the leader of the breakers employed by Cargo, but the arrival of Jiron threw everything into chaos and cost him that position. From then on, he constantly schemed to achieve two goals: to defeat Jiron, and to win the heart of Elche, who had rejected him but whom he continued to love. At first he gave the impression of a calm and collected sharp operator, but gradually his sloppiness became more and more apparent. In the latter half, his trademark became taking out his frustrations on his partner Geraba whenever he failed. Though he had no part to play in the final battle, he appeared properly in the last scene, making sure to show that he was still going strong.',
        119: 'Subordinate, partner, and junior to Hora. Despite his intimidating appearance and physical strength, and his skill at piloting Walker Machines, he is surprisingly timid and cannot defy Hora, who once defeated him. He pulled off the bold move of infiltrating the Iron Gear while pretending to abandon Hora, and abducting Elche. His acting ability on that occasion makes one cannot help but think he could stand on his own even without teaming up with Hora. He had no part in the final battle, but his appearance at the very end was, indeed, just like Hora.',
        120: 'Wife of the transporter Karas Karas. Her charm, emanating from her overly voluptuous figure, was so powerful that even Jiron was overwhelmed, and not a few Breakers fell victim to the passionate kiss she gave as a token of gratitude. When she was shot down during the attack on the Iron Gear, Karas believed her dead and launched a revenge battle, but was instead defeated. This led to the complicated turn of events where she herself now sought to avenge her husband, and thereafter she persistently targeted the Iron Gear. In the end, following the advice of Elche, freed from mental control, she resolved to live on to find new love.',
        121: "The supreme authority of the Innocent. He is 17 years old. The name is hereditary, not his real name. Betrayed by his aide Kashim, he was imprisoned at Yop Point until rescued by Jiron and the others. Afterwards, he declared to all the Innocent that he would overthrow Kashim. The Innocent cannot survive long in outside air, and his resulting frailty, his innocent personality, and above all his beauty made Rag, Birin, and Maria smitten with him. When Elche suffered from Kashim's personality being transplanted into her, he ordered that it be transferred into his own body to save her. And when he realized he could not suppress the Kashim within, he took his own life. However, at the end of the theatrical version, for some reason he appears healthy and lively, exciting the women greatly.",
        122: "A Newtype boy who joins the AEUG, and pilot of the Z Gundam. He is 17. Originally an ordinary, somewhat sensitive boy attending high school in the space colony Green Noa. He had a complex about his feminine name Kamille, and leaned toward masculine hobbies such as Homo Avis (simple gliders) and karate. Perhaps aided by his parents being Federation technical officers, he was also proficient with machinery, skilled enough to win the Junior Mobile Suit competition. However, when Jerid insulted his name and he got into a scuffle with him, he came into conflict with the Titans. He ended up helping Quattro's plan to seize the Gundam Mk-II, and joined the AEUG as a result. In battle, his Newtype abilities awakened, and he gradually came to be active as an ace pilot of the AEUG. Initially fighting simply out of resentment toward the Titans, he grew greatly as a person through his encounters and partings with adults such as Quattro and Amuro, and women such as Four and Rosamia. And while seeking a way to end the war, he came to race through space by his own will. At the end of the TV version, his spirit was dragged down by Scirocco, leaving deep wounds on his heart. But at the end of the theatrical version, he cast that aside and confirmed each other's safety with Fa.",
        123: "One of the central figures who built the foundation of the AEUG. His rank is captain. He is 27. A mysterious man who wears sunglasses that conceal his true face. His true identity is Char Aznable, the Red Comet of the Principality of Zeon, who went missing after the end of the One Year War. Incidentally, 'Quattro' is the Italian word for the number 4, meaning it is his fourth name, following his real name Casval, his alias on Earth Edwou, and his alias in the Principality of Zeon, Char. At first, he used his high mobile suit piloting skills to fight on the front lines in a Rick Dias and the Hyaku Shiki. But his reunion with Amuro and the assassination of AEUG chairperson Blex, among other things, led him to stand on the political stage as a leader. In the final phase, he engaged in a one-on-one duel with Haman on the stage of the Colony Laser, but due to the performance difference between the mobile suits, his machine was wrecked. He vanished into the explosion, and went missing once again.",
        126: "A bridge crew member of the Argama who has joined the AEUG. He is a cheerful and easygoing character. His main role is the ship's navigation and communications/sensor operations, and he is on good terms with Saegusa, whose seat is next to his and who performs nearly the same duties. In the TV version, he once got into a fight with Kamille after teasing him and was ordered to go to the study room.",
        127: "A bridge crew member of the Argama. His main role is the ship's navigation and steering. He is on good terms with Torres, whose seat is next to his and who performs nearly the same duties. At the end of the theatrical version, he was still handling navigation during the quiet conversation in which Kamille and Fa confirmed each other's presence.",
        128: "Originally a member of the Titans, she defected to the AEUG after witnessing Basque's despicable tactics. Her rank remained lieutenant. Her high piloting skill was evidently valued within the AEUG, as she was entrusted with main units such as the Rick Dias, the Gundam Mk-II, and the Super Gundam, and she handled them skillfully. She possessed strong will, acting on her own convictions, along with a soldier's strictness. Yet at the same time, she also had a feminine gentleness. Though she always gave Henken a cold shoulder in response to his advances, in truth she was not entirely indifferent to him. In the final battle against the Titans, after Reccoa was shot down, she exited her immobilized mobile suit and was struck across the body by debris fragments from Yazan's bombardment. Afterward, entrusting her final words to Kamille, who rushed to her side, she passed away in his arms.",
        131: 'A former member of the AEUG, now an officer in the Titans with the rank of ensign. She sought solace in Quattro, but his attitude and words made her realize she was not needed, and she despaired. Then she met Scirocco during a mission, was drawn to him, and defected to the Titans. From then on, she ceased the spy activities she had conducted during her AEUG days and devoted herself to piloting the Palas Athena. During the final battle, she fought Emma, who was also a turncoat but on the opposite side. She heavily damaged the Gundam Mk-II but had her own mobile suit shot down, and she perished hating men to the very end.',
        132: "A subordinate of Quattro who joined the AEUG. His rank was lieutenant. He had originally served in the Principality of Zeon and had participated in the One Year War. He was one of the few veteran pilots aboard the Argama and was a good senior to Kamille. Quattro placed great trust in him, and at times he led the mobile suit team in Quattro's place. In both the TV series and the theatrical version, he died shielding Fa's Methuss.",
        133: "Roberto is a subordinate of Quattro in the Anti-Earth Union Group, holding the rank of Lieutenant. He formerly served in the Principality of Zeon and participated in the One Year War. He is one of the few veteran pilots aboard the Argama and served as a good senior to Kamille. He and Apolly are comrades who have faced countless life-and-death situations together, and they often act in tandem. In the television version, he is shot down and killed by Buran's Asshimar while escorting the shuttle that the AEUG pilots use to ascend to space. However, in the theatrical version, he simply disappears without a specific death scene. Although the possibility of survival remains, compared to his partner who even received a surname, he seems to have been rather shortchanged by the theatrical adaptation.",
        134: "Fa is Kamille's childhood friend and is seventeen years old. Her name, when written in kanji, is 'Hanazono Rei'. Because she was an acquaintance of Kamille, who stole the Gundam Mk-II, she was captured along with her parents by Basque. After being rescued by Bright, she joined the AEUG out of defiance toward the Titans and volunteered as a pilot. While struggling with her own lack of skill, she fought through the Gryps Conflict. She has a nurturing personality and has long admonished Kamille about his lifestyle and habits. Kamille apparently found her nagging inwardly tiresome. Perhaps because of this nature, she also became the caretaker for Shinta and Kum, whom Quattro brought aboard the Argama. In the television version, because her beloved Kamille lost his sanity in the final battle, she later left the battlefield to devote herself to his care and nursing. In the theatrical version, however, the two finished the war with their bodies intact, and they were seen rejoicing over each other's safety.",
        135: "Katz is a boy soldier who joins the AEUG. During the One Year War, because of his connection to boarding the White Base as a refugee, he was raised after the war as the adopted son of Hayato and Fraw's family. However, when his family visited Amuro, he volunteered on his own to join the AEUG and rendezvoused with Amuro aboard the Audhumla. In contrast to his quiet childhood, he became reckless and hot-blooded. He held a rival consciousness toward Kamille, who was the same age, and sometimes sortied without permission or ignored orders. He fell in love with Sara, a subordinate of Scirocco, whom he met on the battlefield, and tried to persuade her to leave his side. But his words were rejected, and worse, he ended up killing her with his own beam. In the final battle against the Titans, he performed a feat of saving Emma from a desperate situation. However, while fleeing from Yazan's grasp, he collided with an asteroid and scattered his young life in space.",
        136: 'Jerid is an officer in the Titans with the rank of Lieutenant and is twenty-four years old. He has a strong sense of elitism and harbors a hidden ambition to seize control of the Titans. He had been walking a smooth path as a soldier, having been selected along with Kacricon and Emma as pilots of the Gundam Mk-II. However, his fate was thrown severely off course by his encounter with Kamille. Initially, he was unfamiliar with handling mobile suits, having crash-landed the Gundam Mk-II and being unable to do anything against Quattro. Yet, perhaps driven by his personal grudge against Kamille, he steadily improved and gradually began to catch the attention of Jamitov and Scirocco. While losing close people one after another - Lila, Kacricon, and Mouar - he kept switching to new machines such as the Marasai, Gabthley, Byarlant, and Baund Doc, relentlessly pursuing Kamille. However, even at the end, he was outmatched, and after his machine was shot through, he was swallowed by the explosion of the Radish. What he attempted to say at the end remains an eternal mystery.',
        137: "Kacricon is an officer in the Titans with the rank of Lieutenant and is twenty-four years old. He was selected along with Jerid and Emma as a pilot of the Gundam Mk-II. He got along well with his colleague Jerid and always acted with him. He is not only skilled at piloting mobile suits but is also a keen strategist with a sharp mind. He apparently had a lover on Earth named Amelia, and when his Varute was slashed open by Kamille's Gundam Mk-II during atmospheric entry, he shouted her name from within the burning wreckage, and those were his final words.",
        138: "Lila Mira Raira was a pilot of a Galbady Beta assigned to the Titans cruiser Bosnia, with the rank of Lieutenant.\nDespite being a woman, she possessed piloting skill enough to serve as the leader of the Galbady unit. With her blunt speech and combative personality, she made no effort to hide her rivalry toward Jerid, whose elitist attitude she dismissed by calling him a 'spoiled little boy.'\nIn the battle against the AEUG as they attempted to descend to Jaburo, she engaged Kamille's Gundam Mk-II. She was shot down without being able to lay a hand on Kamille, who had only recently begun piloting a mobile suit.\nUnlike the TV version, where she saw potential in Jerid to become a fine man, her role was greatly altered in the theatrical version. In the battle against Scirocco, she appeared among the figures floating around Kamille, but...",
        139: 'Bran Bulltaak was a member of the Titans who served concurrently as the captain of the Garuda and the pilot of an Asshimar, with the rank of Major.\nHe was excellent both as a commander and as a pilot, and enjoyed the strong trust of his subordinates. His arrogant and haughty demeanor was a reflection of confidence backed by real ability.\nHe detested the instability of enhanced humans and reportedly viewed Rosamia, who had been assigned to his unit, with distaste.\nTasked with the mission to eliminate the Audhumla, he pursued Kamille and the others on numerous occasions.\nHe fought Kamille and Quattro simultaneously and showed his high skill, more than holding his own against them. In the end, however, he was defeated by the combined efforts of Amuro and Kamille.',
        140: "Ben Woodder was Bran's adjutant, and when Bran sortied, he took command of combat operations aboard the Garuda.\nAfter Bran's death, he assumed the captaincy of the Garuda and attempted to avenge Bran using Four's Psycho Gundam. However, he appeared to be skeptical of the very existence of enhanced humans.\nAfter the battle in Hong Kong, he finally resolved to carry out a suicide attack against the Audhumla using a Garuda-class ship. He issued an order for the crew to abandon ship, but the fact that some remained despite the order suggests he was deeply trusted by his subordinates.",
        141: "Rosamia Badam was an enhanced human trained at the Augusta Research Institute, with the nominal rank of Second Lieutenant.\nShe had lost her family in the colony drop during the One Year War, and that trauma was exploited to perform mental reinforcement on her. However, the repeated experiments and the side effects of the enhancement left her mind unstable.\nShe was incorporated into Bran's unit and frequently engaged Kamille in her Gaplant.\nIn the TV version, she was implanted with false memories of being Kamille's sister, but ultimately suffered a mental breakdown and died at Kamille's hands. In the theatrical version, however, after being shot down at Hickory, she had no explicit death scene and appeared as a spirit in the finale, bearing part of the Z Gundam's power.",
        142: "Four Murasame was an enhanced human trained at the Murasame Research Institute and the pilot of the Psycho Gundam, with the nominal rank of Second Lieutenant.\nOrdinarily gentle and mild-mannered, when she boarded the Psycho Gundam she came under the influence of its mental control waves, transforming into a violent personality accompanied by intense headaches.\nShe had lost her memories of the past, and that loss was a deep complex that bound her tightly. The name Four was not her real name; it merely meant she was the fourth test subject at the Murasame Institute. Yet she believed the words that defeating the Gundam Mk-II would restore her memories, and endured her headaches to keep sitting in the Psycho Gundam's cockpit.\nThrough meeting Kamille, she came into contact with the warmth of the human heart, but upon learning he was the Gundam Mk-II pilot, she fell into anguish.\nIn both the TV and theatrical versions, she lost her life amid the flames of war. In either case, it was the result of throwing herself into danger for Kamille's sake, breaking free of her shackles, so perhaps it was her true wish.",
        143: 'Mauer Pharao was an officer of the Titans with the rank of junior lieutenant. She met Jerid while escaping from Jaburo, and as they began to work together, she came to love both him and his abilities. Her piloting skill was solid, backed by calm judgment and decisive action. Her talent was noticed by Scirocco, but she refused his offer, as she saw him as a danger. She continued to support Jerid, who burned with the desire to defeat Kamille, and died protecting him from an attack by the Z Gundam.',
        144: "Yazan Gable was an officer of the Titans. His initial rank was lieutenant, but he was later promoted to captain. He had a belligerent personality and truly enjoyed war, where he could wield his own power freely. As a pilot, he displayed exceptional skill, maneuvering high-mobility mobile suits such as the Gaplant and Hambrabi as if they were extensions of his own body, and he repeatedly troubled the mobile suit team of the Argama. He possessed the cunning and cruelty to murder even his superiors without hesitation if it was inconvenient for him. However, he also had a caring side, and he seemed to be trusted deeply by his subordinates, including Rumsas and Dunkel. His wickedness, which culminated in taking the lives of Katz and Emma and even laughing aloud, triggered the activation of the biosensor in Kamille's Z Gundam. His machine was destroyed by overwhelming power, and he barely escaped, but he was left adrift in space.",
        145: "Dunkel Cooper was an officer of the Titans and a member of the Hambrabi unit commanded by Yazan. His skill as a pilot was solid, and through coordinated attacks he troubled the Argama on numerous occasions, but in the final phase of the war he was shot down and killed by Kamille's Z Gundam.",
        146: "Rumsas Hasa was an officer of the Titans and a member of the Hambrabi unit commanded by Yazan. Though he had a rough personality, his skill as a pilot was genuine. This can be seen from the fact that even Yazan trusted him enough to recruit him as a subordinate and provide him with a new mobile suit. He persistently pursued the Argama, but in the final phase of the Gryps War, he was shot down and killed along with Dunkel by Emma's Gundam Mk-II.",
        147: 'Sara Zabirov was a Newtype candidate of the Titans with the rank of sergeant. She was drawn to Scirocco, who recognized her worth, and swore absolute loyalty to him. Though the words of Kamille and Katz moved her heart, she never left his side. In the three-way battle among the AEUG, the Titans, and Axis, she died when she intercepted with her own mobile suit a beam that Katz had fired at Scirocco. In the theatrical version, her spirit afterward protected Katz from an enraged Scirocco, suggesting that her feelings for Katz had swayed her considerably.',
        148: "Papetimus Scirocco, captain of the Jupiter fleet ship Jupitris under the Earth Federation government, held the rank of lieutenant and was 26 years old. Possessing high Newtype ability and charisma, he was a genius who could perfectly handle everything from mobile suit design to piloting, strategy planning and command, to the handling of women. His power captivated Sara, caused Reccoa to defect from the Anti-Earth Union Group, and even drew the notoriously picky Yazan to his side. He openly stated that 'after the war, women will rule the world,' but the true meaning of those words remained unclear until the end. After returning to the Earth Sphere, he joined the Titans, but the ambition born of his talent could not be contained within the framework of the military, and he seized control of the Titans by assassinating Jamitov amid the confusion. In the end, he boarded the Zeta Gundam's rival, The O, which he had designed himself, and engaged in a fierce battle with Kamille. However, before the power of the souls surrounding Kamille, he was utterly defeated.",
        149: "Basque Om was the trusted subordinate of Jamitov, founder of the Titans, and effectively the supreme military commander, holding the rank of colonel at age 37. To compensate for his weakened eyesight, he always wore goggles resembling swimming goggles. It is said this condition was a lingering effect of torture suffered when he was taken prisoner by the Principality of Zeon during the One Year War. His personality was cruel and merciless toward anyone outside the Titans, especially Spacenoids. He used poison gas against colonies and took hostages to recover the Gundam Mk-II, stopping at nothing to achieve his goals. He was truly a man who symbolized the Titans. Even after Jamitov's assassination by Scirocco, he attempted to resist independently, but was betrayed and destroyed along with the Dogos Gear by Yazan's Hambrabi, vanishing into the void of space.",
        150: "Jamaican Daningan was a subordinate of Basque, who commanded the Titans, serving as his adjutant with the rank of major. He was a capable commander, but he held elitist beliefs and an arrogant personality. In reality, however, he was a coward who only watched his superior's mood, and as a result he did not enjoy the trust of his subordinates. His end was also miserable: Yazan, who found his existence troublesome, set him up, and a Super Gundam piloted by Emma, guided by the deception, struck his ship's bridge directly.",
        151: 'Jamitov Hymem was a founding member of the Titans and its current supreme commander, holding the rank of general. He was a dangerous man who, while hostile to Spacenoids, even contemplated purging Earthnoids who polluted the Earth. He made the Titans his own tool to that end, but ironically, those who disapproved of his high-handed methods joined forces and gave rise to the Anti-Earth Union Group, his greatest obstacle. He and Blex, the leader of the AEUG, had long been political rivals. He had his trusted subordinate Basque command the Titans while deliberately releasing the dangerous element Scirocco within the organization to stimulate it. But as an Oldtype, he could never hope to control Scirocco, and in the end he was assassinated. Even his death was used by Scirocco to seize control of the Titans.',
        154: "Blex Forer was the leader of the Anti-Earth Union Group, holding the rank of commodore at age 58. A high-ranking officer of the Earth Federation Forces and a member of the Federation Congress, he organized the AEUG out of concern over the rise of the Titans and policies that disregarded the Earth's environment. He had a gentle personality and flexible thinking that included understanding of Newtypes, and he placed expectations on Kamille as well. While attending the Federation Congress in Dakar, he was assassinated by Jamitov's machinations, and with his dying breath entrusted his legacy to Quattro, who carried on the will of Zeon.",
        155: "Henken Bekkener was a central figure of the AEUG, holding the rank of Lieutenant Commander. He was the first captain of the Argama, but when Bright joined the AEUG, he handed over that post and became the captain of the Radish. Although he had spent many years in the military, he retained a certain human warmth that endeared him to his crew, who trusted him deeply. He had also participated in the One Year War and claimed to have felt the pressure of the Red Comet on the battlefield. He harbored feelings of affection for Emma and often showed a pure-hearted side around her. During the final battle against the Titans, in order to protect Emma's Gundam Mk-II which had fallen into a dire situation, he used the Radish as a shield and shared his fate with the ship as it was blown apart.",
        156: "Astonaige Medos was the chief mechanic aboard the Argama, holding the rank of Sergeant. His skill was as reliable as his position suggested, and his presence ensured that the Argama's Mobile Suit teams could always fight at full readiness. In the TV series, he was also an unsung hero who sent Kamille's concepts to Anaheim Electronics, playing a key role in the completion of the Z Gundam; however, this aspect was not depicted in the theatrical version. His talents were evidently well regarded, as he later served as a mechanic under Bright during the Second Neo Zeon War.",
        160: "Haman Karn was the regent of Axis, a resource asteroid where remnants of the Principality of Zeon's military had gathered, though in practice she was the leader who commanded the entire force. Her personality was fierce and cold-blooded. Using Mineva, the orphaned child of Dozle Zabi, as her banner, she championed the revival of Zeon and possessed considerable political acumen, elevating the weak Axis faction into a major power. Her Mobile Suit piloting skills and abilities as a Newtype were also exceptional, and she sometimes took to the front lines herself in custom machines such as the Gaza C and the Qubeley. She had a past history with Quattro and held complex feelings toward him that could be called both love and hatred. When Quattro's Hyaku Shiki was consumed in an explosion at the end of their duel, she murmured her feelings aloud with a lonely air.",
        162: "Loran Cehack was a 17-year-old boy of the Moonrace and the pilot of the Turn A Gundam. Along with Keith and Fran, he had descended to Earth two years prior as an advance scout for the Earth Return Operation. On that occasion, he was saved from drowning in a river by the Heim sisters, and through that connection he came to work at the Heim family's mine, eventually becoming a servant. He had a gentle disposition and disliked conflict, but in order to stop the war between the Moon and Earth, he reluctantly joined the Ingressa Militia. Despite his personality, he was highly skilled at piloting Mobile Suits, and combined with the performance of the Turn A Gundam, he was a core asset of the Militia. In situations where he faced enemies on foot while armed, he also showed a manly side, fighting bravely without hesitation. Like other Moonrace, he was devoted to Dianna, and her well-being was always his first priority in his actions. After the final confrontation with Ghingnham, he stepped into a new life together with Dianna, who had remained on Earth after swapping places with Kiel.",
        164: "Kiel Heim was the eldest daughter of the Heim family, for whom Loran worked as a servant, and was 17 years old. Unbound by feudal social conventions, she believed that women should advance into the wider society, and she served as an aide to Guin. She bore such a striking resemblance to the Moon Queen Dianna that even her own family could not tell them apart. At Dianna's suggestion, they began swapping places half in jest, but the timing to switch back was lost, and she ended up truly placed in the position of queen. That turn of events led her to realize that the Moonrace were no different from Earthlings, and she came to strive to understand Dianna's thinking and to consider what she herself should do. Harry, who was the first to notice the swap, protected her at the risk of his own life, and as they shared the secret together, she came to develop feelings for him. When she confessed her love, she appeared as a girl of her age. After peace was restored, she swapped back with Dianna and, before the Moonrace, claimed the name Dianna.",
        165: "Dianna Soreil is the head of the Soreil family that rules the Moon, and the queen of the Moonrace. She is the emotional anchor for the Moonrace, and commands overwhelming trust and respect. Her stated age is 19, but due to repeated artificial hibernation, several hundred years have passed since her birth. During that time she has visited Earth several times, and those experiences became the major driving force behind the return to Earth. By chance she met Kiel, who had an identical appearance, and while swapping places on a whim, she lost the opportunity to switch back. However, while living among Earth's people as Kiel, she came to learn their true feelings, and learned about the true nature of peace and how to achieve it. And at last, she came to know that the true enemy she must fight was Agrippa. After defeating Agrippa and Ghingnham, she remained on Earth and gained a happy life living in nature alongside Loran.",
        166: 'Milan Rex was an administrator who descended to Earth with Dianna, serving as a sort of deputy. He seemed to be a gentle and rational person, but when Phil rebelled in an attempt to seize control of the Dianna Counter, he sided with the military. This appeared to be a painful decision made to deal with various problems, such as the slow-moving diplomacy and food shortages. Deep in his heart, his loyalty to Dianna remained rooted, and when Dianna returned to Earth, he once again became her subject. After the battle with Ghingnham, he followed Dianna (Kiel) and returned to the Moon.',
        167: "Sochie Heim is the second daughter of the Heim family, for whom Loran worked as a servant. She is 15 years old. Her personality is competitive, spirited, and tomboyish. She is interested in Loran, but due to their positions and her temperament, she cannot be honest about it. To avenge her father, who was killed in an attack by the Dianna Counter, she volunteered for the Ingressa Militia and became a Kapool pilot. Because of that, she was initially hardened with hatred toward the Moonrace. But through learning Loran's true identity and the incident with Gavane, who loved her and even proposed to her, she grew greatly as a person. In the end, her feelings for Loran were never fulfilled, and she exchanged a tearful farewell kiss with Loran, who chose to go with Dianna. Afterwards, she threw Loran's goldfish toy into the river, parting with her own feelings.",
        168: "Meshee Kuhn was born into a family of airplane makers going back to her grandfather's generation, and she herself flies through the sky as an airplane pilot. She is 18 years old. She belonged to the airplane unit of the Ingressa Militia and had been fighting since the start of the war. She and Sochie were close enough to be called best friends, and after the Kapool was excavated, they often rode into battle together. When she went up to the Moon, she became friendly with a boy soldier of the Dianna Counter, and sortied together with him in a WaD. Her relationship with this boy seems to have continued even after the war ended.",
        170: "Corin Nander is a former sergeant of the Dianna Counter. After being defeated by Loran, he entered the priesthood and wandered from place to place, but when he saw the light of the M-Fly released by Merrybell's Turn A Gundam, he remembered his own mission. He headed to Dianna, and when he was permitted to return to the military and to defeat the Turn-type Gundam, he was so moved that he wept. His reckless behavior continued as before, such as having a Kapool repainted in his own custom colors, much to the amazement of those around him. But his skill had not declined, and he performed aerial combat in the unfamiliar Kapool, overwhelming the Mahiroo unit. Eventually, when the Turn X also activated its M-Fly, he deliberately stole fuel from the Kapools of Sochie and Meshee, leaving the two of them far from the battlefield, and went alone to his death.",
        171: "Joseph Yott was a young man of 23 who worked as a disciple of the mountain prospector Sid, involved in excavation work at the Mountain Cycle. He was born into the minority Maba tribe, and in his childhood his parents were killed in tribal conflict; he was abandoned in the mountains and taken in by Sid. Because of this past, he harbored a rivalry that could be called hostility toward North Americans and Moonrace alike, and his attitude toward Loran was especially harsh. His abundant knowledge of machinery was recognized, and he joined the Militia's mobile suit unit, coming to command the Jarapee (junk vehicle) squad. While fighting aboard the flat that Loran and the others used during their descent to Earth, he grew close to Fran, who had taught him how to pilot it. After peace came, he seems to have quit the prospector's trade for the sake of his family, and he was seen carrying the child he had with Fran while working hard at his new job as a fishmonger.",
        172: 'Sid Munza was an old man called a mountain prospector - an excavator and also a researcher of the Black History. Together with his disciple Joseph, he excavated Kapools and other artifacts from the Mountain Cycle. Because he had taken command of excavating weapons, he came to accompany the Militia. He flew around excavation sites without sparing sleep, and when manpower was short he would board a Borjarnon to intercept the enemy, showing vitality beyond his years in every scene. His trademark was a helmet with an attached flashlight that made him look like a frog and seemed convenient for excavation work. After the fighting ended, he returned to prospecting with Poe, who appeared to have been taken on as a new disciple in place of Joseph, who had started a family.',
        173: "Guin Sard Rheinford was the grandson of the Ingressa lord and a central figure of the Ingressa Militia. He was 19 years old. Though raised as a young master, he had no sense of being naive about the world, and showed a tenacity to use whatever could be used, along with excellent negotiation skills, political acumen, and judgment, all of which were further honed through battle. Even when confronted with the Moonrace's overwhelming technology, he was not crushed, but instead secretly planned to use that technology to bring about an industrial revolution. Even when Ingressa fell and he lost power, he resolved to climb back up from there - an ambitious man with resilience. He had a strong fixation on Loran, calling him 'Laura' and making him dress in women's clothing. Even when he betrayed Dianna, he tried to bring only Loran over to his side, and this obsession went somewhat beyond the bounds of reason. In the epilogue, he was confirmed to have crossed to Gallia together with Merrybell, whom he had saved with his own hands.",
        174: "Michael Guern was the commander of the Ingressa Militia, with the rank of colonel. He was 35 years old. He believed that the Moonrace were invaders of Earth and that fighting them was a matter of defending his homeland. For this reason, he seemed displeased that Guin, whom he considered a mere figurehead, viewed the war as nothing more than one means of negotiation. However, he was tossed about by the rapidly changing situation and by Guin's drive in formulating strategies to match it, and in the end he followed along all the way to the final battle. But when the Willgem crashed down and Guin's ambitions came to an end, he at the same time abandoned him and went his own way.",
        175: "Gavane Gooney was the captain of the Sue Sai Do squad, the elite mobile suit unit of the Luzan Militia. He was 27 years old. He had a cheerful personality, but on the battlefield he was a valiant commander who always led from the front, earning deep trust from his subordinates. He had a flexible mind, changing tactics to suit the situation. When he first met the Ingressa Militia, he treated Loran and the others with derision, calling them 'Ingressa bastards' and challenging the Turn A Gundam to a test of strength. But as they fought together, he came to acknowledge them as comrades in arms. In particular, he was drawn to Sochie, whom he called 'young miss', by her single-minded way of fighting, and he went so far as to propose to her. However, while fighting the Red squad in the underground tunnels of Lost Mountain over the excavated nuclear bomb, he vanished into the light of a nuclear blast that went off by accident. Every one of his comrades mourned his death and shed tears.",
        176: "Lili Borjano is the thirteenth and youngest daughter of Duke Borjano, lord of Rujan. Her personality is selfish and naive about the world, and her lighthearted inability to comprehend war is just like a young lady of privilege. However, she possesses extraordinary insight into matters and keen observational skills for judging a person's true character. She had known Guin since childhood, and was seen harassing Kiel, who was acting as Dianna, when she approached him. Eventually, however, she came to admire Kiel, who served as Queen of the Moon in Dianna's place, and offered to become her friend. When she was betrayed by Guin, she showed no sign of being shaken, and instead displayed a strong core by attempting to stop his actions. She once even proposed to Loran, saying 'Become Laura and seduce Guin.' This may have been a reflection of her wounded heart, stemming from being disregarded as a woman.",
        177: "Horace Nyben is a Moonrace engineer. Initially he worked alongside the Dianna Counter that had accompanied him, but he defected to Earth, driven by his intellectual curiosity toward the excavated Earth weapons. Afterwards, at Guin's request, he came to cooperate with the Ingressa Militia. There were many places where he could demonstrate his abilities, including the research, analysis, repair, and maintenance of excavated weapons such as the Turn A Gundam. Although most Moonrace engineers were not well-regarded by Earthlings, he seemed not to care much, perhaps because he was only interested in unknown technology. He had a distinctive face like a great Buddha statue, and Merrybell, who had a panda-like face, called it an 'interesting face.' After the war ended, he remained on Earth and helped with the restoration of the Willgem.",
        178: "Harry Ord serves as the captain of the Dianna Guard. He is 18 years old and holds the rank of lieutenant, later being promoted to captain. His personality is calm and intellectual, but he is too earnest, giving him an inflexible side. He has sworn absolute loyalty to Dianna, and his devotion is so famous that even ordinary female soldiers know of it. He was the first to notice the switch between Dianna and Kiel, but he continued to serve without changing his attitude, and protected Kiel. He always wears red sunglasses that serve as night-vision goggles, which he himself says are 'to hide his gaze when looking at women other than Dianna.' He did not even remove them when kissing Kiel, who had developed feelings for him, but it seems this did not cause her to fall out of favor with him. His skill in piloting his gold-colored custom SUMO is superbly top-class. At the Winter Palace, he took on the Mahiroo unit led by Suesson with a single machine and defeated them in seconds, which shows his true ability. He favored wearing yellow-and-black suits and vests, and pajamas with star patterns, leaving his fashion sense questionable. After the battle with Ghingnham ended, and Kiel once again switched places with Dianna and crossed to the Moon, Harry was at her side as always.",
        179: "Meem Midgard is a Moonrace who infiltrated Earth on Agrippa's orders, holding the rank of captain. While serving as the manager of Keith's bread factory as a cover, he plotted the assassination of Dianna and the seizure of the Turn A Gundam. His personality is sullen and suspicious, and when he judged that Teteth, who had been ordered to assassinate Dianna, had failed her mission, he shot her dead to silence her. The marksmanship he displayed at that time was considerable. After returning to the Moon, he committed outrages such as engaging in battle involving the Winter Palace, where many citizens were in cryogenic sleep. However, these actions became the trigger for activating the M-Fly. In the end, he shot his superior Agrippa, and was then killed by the hand of Harry's SUMO, receiving 'the judgment of Dianna's law.'",
        180: "Teteth Halle is a woman who plotted the assassination of Dianna on Midgard's orders. She was born to a woman Dianna had brought back from Earth to the Moon, and a Moonrace man. Having grown up facing discrimination from an early age, she harbored intense hatred toward everything around her - Dianna, the Moon's system, and Earthling blood. As a reward for the assassination, she had secured a promise from Midgard to make her an honorary citizen of the Moon. The plan failed, however, and she was shot dead by Midgard, who feared the matter would come to light. Later, a scene was broadcast showing her mother Linda waking from cryogenic sleep and searching for her daughter, which only emphasized the tragedy further.",
        181: "Phil Ackman was a lieutenant in the Dianna Counter. After the death of his senior officer, he became the commander of the Earth descent operation. He looked down on Earthlings as barbarians and advocated for subjugation by military force. However, taking advantage of Dianna's departure from Earth due to her desire for peaceful coexistence, he turned traitor and declared the founding of the Sunbelt Republic. At one point he even showed ambition to become the king of Earth, but in the end he swore loyalty to Dianna once more. He then united even with the Earth side, which still harbored ill feelings, and fought against the Ghingnham fleet. After the fighting was over, he returned to the Moon together with Dianna (Kiel) and the others.",
        182: "Poe Eiji was a second lieutenant in the Dianna Counter. She descended to Earth as a pilot of a Wodom under Phil's command. Her interception of the Militia's airplane squadron became the opening of the long-standing conflict between Earth and the Moon. She was quick to tears and wept at every turn, and this tearfulness even became the subtitle of episode 31. She appeared to be in a romantic relationship with her superior Phil, and she followed him when he raised his banner of rebellion against Dianna. Yet deep in her heart, loyalty to the Queen was rooted, and when Dianna returned she once again shed tears of joy. After all the battles were over, she could be seen taking on Mountain Cycle alongside Sid, perhaps having become his apprentice.",
        183: "Ghingnham Gym was the head of the Ghingnham family, which governed the martial arts of the Moonrace, and the supreme commander of the Ghingnham space fleet. True to his words, 'Combat is the very reason for my existence,' he always carried a sword and personally boarded the Turn X to go to the front lines. This behavior stemmed from his intense pride in being a man of the warrior class. Usually he was calm and held broad-minded views, but once battle began, he revealed his arrogant and belligerent true nature. As a result, he became so excited that he lost sight of his surroundings, exposing his battle mania by attacking friend and foe alike without distinction. The greatest reason he opposed Dianna was his resentment that she had ignored him and his people, who had repeated exercises for 2500 years, and had independently organized the Dianna Counter to descend to Earth. Conversely, this also served as proof of his strong loyalty to Dianna. Against Loran's Turn A Gundam, which he recognized as his sworn enemy, he fought to a draw even in the final battle, with both machines destroyed. Mere moments after escaping, he then faced Loran in personal combat with swords, but during that struggle he was swallowed by the cocoon of the Moonlight Butterfly and returned to the Earth along with the two Turn-type machines.",
        184: "Suesson Stello was the captain leading the Mahiroo squadron of the Ghingnham fleet. He was a man full of faults: rough in personality, base in character, and calmly imposing unreasonable demands on his subordinates. It was no wonder Midgard described him as 'a water blister riding on the prestige of a distinguished family.' His fighting style was also lacking in flexibility, as he could only perform by-the-book maneuvers due to having done nothing but drills within the fleet. His end was a pitiful one: he cut into a battle between Turn-type machines, incurred Ghingnham's wrath, and was shot down by him.",
        185: "Merrybell Gadget was a girl said to be Ghingnham's puppet. She came from the lowest class of the Moon's society and had a past of being taken in by Ghingnham. Her appearance - eccentric clothing that also served as a spacesuit, large earmuffs, eye makeup, and bells on her head - along with her physical agility, such as doing handstands even on Earth with six times the Moon's gravity, evoked the image of a clown. She preferred to be near highly capable and amusing individuals such as Ghingnham and Guin. And she would toss words to them that incited war. Despite what her words suggested, she possessed mobile suit piloting skill beyond imagination and manipulated the Bandit as if it were an extension of her own body. Her coordination with unmanned mobile suits apparently relied on a special ability of hers, but the details were unknown. In the epilogue she was seen acting alongside Guin, and it was then that her true face was revealed for the first time.",
        186: "Agrippa Maintainer was the head of the Maintainer family, which had managed the Winter Palace, the artificial cryogenic sleep facility of the Moonrace. As the administrative official in charge of the internal affairs of the lunar capital Gengannam, he was well-versed in the Turn A Gundam and the Black History.\nHe had set the maintenance of the lunar society's tranquility and peace as his supreme objective, and feared that contact with the Earthlings would awaken the instinct for combat in the hearts of the Moonrace. For this reason, he opposed the Earth descent operation, and carried out various acts of sabotage, such as delaying supplies and plotting the assassination of Dianna. However, at the end of his argument with Dianna and the others, he was struck down by Midgard's bullet.",
        187: "Keith Laijie was a Moonrace youth who, along with Loran and Fran, had descended to Earth two years prior as an advance surveyor for the return to Earth. He was 17 years old.\nHe had been working as an apprentice at the Nocis bakery Donkey. However, when the Dianna Counter descended, he took over the shop along with the owner's daughter Bellene after the owner was injured.\nHe sold the flat he had used for the descent to the Ingressa Militia, and with that money built a bread factory, actively employing Moonrace who had fled. This positive attitude of doing his best with what he could do greatly contributed to the bridge between Earth and the Moon at the civilian level.\nWhether it was the fruit of his efforts or not, his bread-making skills were wonderful, and its taste was very popular with both Earthlings and the Moonrace.\nIn the epilogue, the child he had with Bellene could be confirmed.",
        188: 'Fran Doll was a Moonrace girl who, along with Loran and Keith, had descended to Earth two years prior as an advance surveyor for the return to Earth. She was 17 years old.\nShe worked as a printer at the Nocis newspaper company, the Nocis Chronicle, but later achieved her long-held dream of becoming a newspaper reporter. She always considered the significance of reporting, and never cowered in the face of war, striving to convey the truth. Even when she learned that her articles were being suppressed by news blackouts, she did not stop fulfilling her duties as a reporter.\nShe came to know Joseph by chance, and eventually became close enough with him that she could speak her true feelings and act spoiled in front of him. By the time of the final battle, she was carrying his child. And in the epilogue, the two of them can be seen walking through life together.',
        189: "Garrod Ran was a boy who survived the devastated world by his own power, without relying on others. He was 15 years old.\nHe was a war orphan, but had a bright and forward-looking personality that did not feel tragic. Perhaps because his father had been a military scientist, he excelled at handling machinery in general. Behind that, he may have harbored the desire to become an engineer like his father. Before boarding the Freeden, he used his innate resourcefulness and cunning to hunt mobile suits and sell them to junk dealers, living toughly. Perhaps learned from such a life, he could open the locks of the Freeden's interior and the Bradman residence's doors with just a piece of wire.\nHis mobile suit piloting skills were genius-level, and he quickly mastered the Gundam X and Gundam Double X on his first time piloting them. Even in his first battle in space, he grasped the knack in an extremely short time. His high adaptability was so great that Lancelow, who witnessed it, could not hide his surprise.\nDuring a certain job, he met the Newtype girl Tiffa and fell in love at first sight. From then on, he continued to show a single-minded devotion, plunging into fire or water, on the sea or in space, anywhere, regardless of danger, for her sake. That feeling was eventually recognized by D.O.M.E. and became a great power that brought the war to an end.\nThough self-proclaimed, his nickname 'The Flame Mobile Suit Pilot' accurately described him, for better or worse.\nAfter the war, he set out on a journey with Tiffa, to go to various places, see various things, and meet many people, in order to think about what kind of future he himself was seeking.",
        190: "Tiffa Adill was a naturally awakened Newtype girl born after the 7th Space War, who was whispered to not exist. She was 15 years old.\nShe displayed powers that could be called psychic abilities, such as future vision, danger detection, and extreme sensitivity (the Newtypes of 'Gundam X' have a different meaning from the Newtypes of previous Gundam series).\nMany organizations targeted her as research material for her abilities, and she was confined in a place like a Newtype research facility before being rescued by Jamil and the others. After boarding the Freeden, she became the group's guide, and eventually reached D.O.M.E. on the Moon.\nHer Newtype abilities were sought after endlessly by those around her, but she herself feared that power. Also, because she detested people fighting over this power, she had lived with her heart half-closed. However, she gradually opened her heart to Garrod, who treated her as an individual girl, and eventually she was able to express her feelings outward.\nIn the midst of battle, she wished to be of help to Garrod and the other important people, and the power heightened by that wish became the factor that opened D.O.M.E. on the Moon.\nAfter the Freeden was disbanded, true to her words 'I will be with Garrod,' she departed together with Garrod, who said he wanted to see the world.",
        191: "Jamil Neate is the captain of the Freeden, an organization dedicated to searching for and protecting Newtypes. He is 30 years old. In addition to his tendency not to show emotion, the sunglasses he always wears give him an even more taciturn impression. However, the crew of the Freeden place tremendous trust in their captain, which speaks to his human appeal. During the 7th Space War, he was a Newtype who belonged to the Earth Federation Forces and served as the pilot of the Gundam X. Yet in the final phase of the great war, he pulled the trigger that set off the greatest tragedy in human history, the 'Colony Drop'. That guilt became a trauma, and he lost all of his Newtype abilities. He suffered from a fear of cockpits brought on by his trauma, but through his encounter with Garrod, he overcame it. Thereafter, he piloted the Gundam X Divider and was active in battle. At the end of a long journey, by coming into contact with the D.O.M.E., he finally obtained the future he had been seeking. After the fighting ended, he became a member of the Federation government's peace council alongside Sara, and chose the path of building the world he had dreamed of with his own hands.",
        192: 'Sara Tyrrell is the operator of the Freeden. She is 18 years old. She is a woman in a vice-captain-like position who sometimes serves as acting captain when Jamil is absent. She takes a theoretical approach to thinking and acts accordingly, but at times she could not hold back her emotions and would speak harshly. She harbors feelings for Jamil that go beyond mere respect, and when it came to him, she could not remain calm. She was also seen showing jealousy toward Tiffa, who was still a young girl. Amidst this, Roybea made advances on her, and although her heart wavered between him and Jamil, in the end she stayed true to her feelings for Jamil. After the war ended, she attended the peace talks with the Space Revolutionary Army alongside Jamil as a member of the peace council, where she was introduced as his reliable partner.',
        193: "Toniya Mam is the communications officer of the Freeden. She is 17 years old. She has a bright and friendly personality, and she is the mood maker not only of the bridge but of the entire Freeden. She formed a deep friendship with Ennil, whom she met during their journey, and her natural cheerfulness was a major catalyst in opening up Ennil's closed heart. However, her blunt way of speaking sometimes hurt others, and she once made a flippant remark about Witz's photograph that touched on a painful wound. But that incident became the trigger for her and Witz to gradually grow closer. And before heading into the final battle, they had become close enough that he gave her a ring along with his feelings. After the war ended, she apparently gave him a favorable answer, and she was seen visiting his hometown together with Witz.",
        194: "Shingo Mori is the helmsman of the Freeden. He is 20 years old. His appearance is plain, and his presence is somewhat faint. However, his skill at the helm is first-rate, making him an indispensable member of the Freeden. When he first went into space, he displayed a masterful technique by taking the helm of the Freeden II after merely glancing at the manual. While docked, he also handled various odd jobs, and when Garrod, who had snuck aboard the Freeden, was put in a cell, Shingo served as his guard. After peace came, he was seen running the junk shop 'Freeden III' together with Kid and Pala.",
        195: 'Witz Sou is a mobile suit pilot employed by the Freeden. He is 17 years old. He is manly in various senses, and is the type to act before speaking. His speech is also quite rough. He was originally a freelance mobile suit pilot, and the Gundam Air Master is a keepsake from a Vulture who helped him in the past. At first he gave the impression of a money-grubbing mercenary who fought only for money, but all of it was actually to make life easier for his family back home. His father was killed by a mobile suit pilot in the past, and while his mother, who hates such pilots, cannot be told about his job, he possesses the kindness to keep fighting for his family. He eventually signed an exclusive contract with the Freeden, with which he had various connections. Witz rationalized it by saying that the Freeden was a good place to hide the gold he earned, but it is thought that another reason was that he wanted to be near Toniya, for whom he secretly held feelings. On the night before the final battle, he gave Toniya a ring and confessed his feelings. Later, he brought her back to his hometown, so things apparently went well. But just after that, at the height of his happiness, an unexpected tragedy (or comedy?) began to unfold for Witz.',
        196: "Roybea is a mobile suit pilot hired by the Freeden. He is 18 years old. As a freelance mobile suit pilot, he maintains an easygoing and carefree attitude, saying 'I don't like things that are too ideological.' However, when the Freeden, where he was previously employed, fell into crisis, he rushed to its rescue, and as he himself says, he is 'surprisingly a good guy.' He eventually signed an exclusive contract with the Freeden, with which he had many ties, and began to share its fortunes. At that time, he set up a relaxation room aboard the ship and tried to collect membership fees from the crew. However, due to Sara's conditions, women were free, and no money could be taken from children under 15, so Garrod and Tiffa were also free, and after losing a billiards match, Tex was also free - in the end, he ended up providing free use to almost everyone who would use it. He is flirtatious and frivolous, skilled with both his hands and his tongue, and making passes at women is his hobby. He has girlfriends in various places, and he is diligent enough to find time to visit them, calling it aftercare. However, the woman who was his true love has already passed away, and his beloved mobile suit, the Gundam Leopard, is her memento. His current true love is Sara. He seems to harbor surprisingly sincere feelings for her, and had been making advances on her constantly. Then, right before the final battle, he finally confessed his feelings and asked for her answer. After the war ended, Sara became Jamil's partner, but he displayed his natural playboy nature and subsequently became close with Ennil.",
        197: "Ennil is a freelance mobile suit pilot whose beloved mobile suit is always painted blue. She is 19 years old. She has survived alone in the post-war world using her skills and beauty. Having lived a harsh life driven by the mere act of survival, she has built walls that prevent her from opening her heart to others. She met Garrod when he took the Gundam X from the Freeden, and when he rejected her seduction, her pride was wounded, and from then on she chased after him in a state of misplaced grudge. Later, she met Toniya, who was out in town during half-deck rest, and as their friendship as women deepened, a change was born in her heart. Afterwards, her life was saved by the Freeden, and she subsequently came to cooperate with Garrod as well. In the epilogue, though the circumstances are unknown, she appeared in Witz's hometown together with Roybea, and together with Toniya, the two of them toyed with the menfolk.",
        198: "Kid is the chief mechanic of the Freeden. As can be seen from the fact that he serves as chief at the young age of 12, the youngest of the crew, his mechanical skills and knowledge rival those of adults. He is quite versatile, handling mobile suit maintenance of course, but also creating simulators for bit attacks and adjusting the combining mechanisms of the G Falcon. Jamil never interferes with his work, which suggests he places great trust in Kid. He is constantly stockpiling useful parts and ideas, and it was his handiwork that powered up the various Gundams, including the Gundam X, the Airmaster, and the Leopard. After the Freeden fulfilled its role, he began running a junk shop called 'Freeden III' together with Shingo, Pala, and his subordinate mechanics.",
        199: "Tex is the Freeden's dedicated physician. He is 36 years old. His ability as a doctor is extremely high, and he handles all kinds of work, from internal medicine to surgery, and even mental care. As the oldest of the crew, he possesses deep experience and the composure of an adult. Jamil also trusts him deeply, and he often served as a sounding board for Jamil's concerns. He is quite a bibliophile, and once recited the contents of 'Lorelei' by the German poet Heine. His hobby is billiards, and his skill at this is also considerable; in a match with Roybea wagering the usage fee for the relaxation room, he won a splendid victory. Later, when most of the crew went out for supplies, he tried to conduct secret training, thinking it was a good opportunity, and was seen by Sara and Toniya, panicking - showing an unexpectedly childlike side. After the Freeden was disbanded, he served at a field hospital. He offered a cup to two enemy soldiers arguing with each other and said, 'Most problems can be solved in your heart while drinking one cup of coffee. The rest is just a matter of whether you can put it into action,' showing his adult composure to the very end.",
        200: "Pala is a G Falcon pilot belonging to Saterikon, a resistance organization against the Space Revolutionary Army. She is 15 years old. Her parents, who were space refugees, died soon after she was born. Having grown up in an environment surrounded only by men, she blurts out rough words like 'that's lame' and her speech is crude. Her personality is also extremely boyish, but when Saterikon was annihilated, tears of sadness, and after achieving the destruction of the Colony Laser, her true aspiration, tears of joy flowed down her cheeks. Her face at that time was that of a girl her age. She hit it off with Garrod when she helped him out of a pinch in space, and they came to fight together. Afterwards, when she became a member of the Freeden, she got along with Kid, who was a kindred spirit. After the war ended, she seems to have found a new place for herself at the junk shop 'Freeden III' that she started with Kid, Shingo, and the others.",
        201: "An infamous freelance mobile suit pilot. The elder of the Frost brothers. 19 years old. His career as a freelance mobile suit pilot was a cover; in truth, he was an agent of the New Federation military intelligence agency. He possessed the telepathic ability 'Twins Synchronity,' which allowed him to communicate with his fraternal twin brother Olba without speaking a word. This allowed them to avoid danger for each other and to carry out operations even from distant locations. However, despite possessing such abilities, he was not recognized under Newtype supremacism and was branded with the mark of 'Category F.' As a result, he came to hate Newtypes and all of the world that acknowledged their existence. His personality was cruel and vicious, and he stopped at nothing to achieve his goals. He killed his targets of revenge and those whose use had expired one after another, sometimes with his beloved Gundam Virsago and sometimes by pointing a gun directly at them. He was also always calm and collected, able to accurately assess his surroundings and the tide of battle. He frequently chided Olba, who would lose his head and lose sight of the situation, but during the final battle with Garrod, he forcibly fired a satellite launcher that was insufficiently charged, despite Olba's attempts to stop him. After the war ended, he was seen in a corner of a certain town, pushing Olba's wheelchair while watching Garrod and Tiffa set out on their journey.",
        202: "An infamous freelance mobile suit pilot. The younger of the Frost brothers. 19 years old. His career as a freelance mobile suit pilot was a cover; in truth, he was an agent of the New Federation military intelligence agency. He possessed the telepathic ability 'Twins Synchronity,' which allowed him to communicate with his fraternal twin brother Shagia without speaking a word. This allowed them to avoid danger for each other and to carry out operations even from distant locations. However, despite possessing such abilities, he was not recognized under Newtype supremacism and was branded with the mark of 'Category F.' As a result, he came to hate Newtypes and all of the world that acknowledged their existence. His personality was cold and heartless, and he stopped at nothing to achieve his goals. But that was only his outward face; within him lay a fierce passion unimaginable from his refined features. He was often admonished by Shagia when he lost his head and lost sight of the situation. However, during the final battle with Garrod, a rare scene was seen where he stopped Shagia, who tried to forcibly fire an insufficiently charged satellite launcher. After the war ended, in a corner of a certain town, there was his figure pushing Shagia's wheelchair while watching Garrod and Tiffa set out on their journey.",
        203: "The captain of the Space Revolutionary Army's training battalion. His rank was colonel. 34 years old. He was a Newtype who fought on equal terms with Jamil during the 7th Space War, but after the war ended, he lost that ability. Even 15 years later, he still belonged to the Revolutionary Army and was highly favored by Supreme Leader Seidel. However, he was aware that this was because his former status as a Newtype made him useful to the public as a symbol of the future and to the military as a means of boosting morale. Even without his Newtype powers, his mobile suit piloting skills were top-class. When he engaged Garrod, who had gone into space for Tiffa's sake, he won a complete victory with ease. Eventually, he learned that Jamil was fighting to protect Newtypes, came to understand his actions, and aided Jamil and his group when they were struggling against the Frost brothers. After the war ended, as one of the leaders of the Space Revolutionary Army, he shook hands in friendship with Jamil, who had become a member of the peace council.",
        204: "A military officer belonging to the New Federation. His abilities as a soldier were high enough to serve as the captain of a special forces unit, but he was also a man who caused trouble in various places through insubordination and firing on his superiors. He infiltrated the Freeden disguised as a fisherman, plotting to capture it, but failed and was captured himself instead. Later, taking advantage of the confusion of battle, he seized the bridge and accomplished his goal, but meeting Tiffa brought about a change in his heart. He cooperated with Garrod, who sought to rescue Tiffa from the New Federation's capture, without regard for his own interests, but in the end, he died shielding Garrod and Tiffa from gunfire. Although he claimed to be bad with such things, he spoke of his deceased wife at every turn, revealing the depth of his feelings for the family he had lost in the war.",
        205: "The supreme leader of the Space Revolutionary Army. He advocated the Newtype ideology that 'humanity is first established as a Newtype when space transforms them,' and sought to lead humanity living in space. However, these claims were merely slogans to maintain his own power, and he had no real need for true Newtypes. For that reason, he not only refused to acknowledge Tiffa, a naturally occurring Newtype born and raised on Earth, but even sought to eliminate her. While in the midst of the decisive battle on the Moon to destroy the New Federation and obtain the power of Newtypes, he was led to D.O.M.E. and came into contact with its true nature. However, he could not accept the fact revealed there that 'Newtypes do not exist.' Clinging to his Newtype ideology and attempting to continue the fight, he was shot by the Frost brothers and vanished into space along with his ambitions.",
        206: "The supreme commander of the New Federation Forces. He feared that with the rise of Newtypes, all people including himself would be branded as Oldtypes. He was lifted up by the Frost Brothers as 'one who would become the new leader of the world,' and eventually, guided by them, he fought a decisive battle against the Revolutionary Army on the Moon. Later, through contact with D.O.M.E., he touched upon the true nature of Newtypes, but even so, he did not stop the war. When escaping from D.O.M.E., his insistence on Newtypes to the very end incurred the wrath of the Frost Brothers, and he was blown away along with his ship.",
        207: "A boy who served as the leader of the self-defense corps of the local city Fort Severn. 15 years old. He was an artificial Newtype so excellent that Mayor Nomoa called him 'my greatest masterpiece.' He himself had absolute confidence in his own power, and possessed corresponding ability. He used his beloved Vertigo to drive off the Gundam X, but the existence of Tiffa, a natural Newtype who should not exist, and his defeat by a revived Garrod caused him to lose his sense of purpose. Finally, when he was about to take his own life, Garrod saved him, and that became the catalyst for him to open his heart. Afterwards, his power was exploited by Nomoa, in truth Dorat, and he destroyed the city with Patulia. After Dorat was defeated by Garrod and the others, he resolved to devote himself to the city's reconstruction as atonement. Later, as a unit commander leading one force of the anti-New Federation organization, he saved the crew of the Freeden from crisis. Furthermore, when they needed a means to go into space, he even arranged a space battleship for them. For a while after the war ended, he apparently traveled with Garrod and Tiffa. But his tact in departing alone, saying, 'I cannot keep getting in the way of you two forever,' was worthy of the name of a Newtype.",
        208: "An educational officer of the Old Federation Forces, in charge of instructing the Flash System. She was Jamil's superior during his military days, but to him, she was a woman who meant more than that. At the end of the great war, her hatred of battle and her wish for peace became too strong, causing her to suffer a mental breakdown. The Federation Forces, noticing her Newtype abilities and her hatred of war, used her as the core of the L System, which halted the electronic equipment of weapons. However, the L Operation that was to use it was ultimately canceled. Afterwards, the L System lay at the bottom of the sea, but it was discovered and recovered during the salvage of the G Bits that had sunk at the same time. Lucille within was not completely unconscious; borrowing Tiffa's body, she appeared before Jamil and saved the Freeden from an attack by the Seaburch. She also lent her power to Jamil, who had lost his Newtype abilities, assisting in the control of the G Bits. After the battle was over, when she was reunited with Jamil, at her own request, she sank deep into the sea along with the L System.",
        209: 'The intelligence coordinator of the Government Reconstruction Committee. The man who had the Gundam Double X developed on Zonder Epta Island. He focused on Newtypes, plotting to obtain their power and take control of the committee. He believed he was manipulating the Frost Brothers to suit his own convenience, but in reality, he was merely being used by them in turn. In the end, during the escape from Zonder Epta, he was shot dead by Shagia.',
        210: 'A soldier belonging to the New Federation Forces, with the rank of lieutenant. Originally a skilled pilot, he blossomed his latent Newtype abilities during combat with Garrod, using Bit Mobile Suit tactics to corner Garrod and the others. However, when he temporarily withdrew due to damage, he was struck down by a bullet from Shagia, who hated Newtypes.',
    },
}
